{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"assumptions\":[\"Approved P06 plan is authoritative for the bounded API and protected-file scope.\",\"Existing P03/P04 modules are reference integrations; the new runtime will avoid changing them.\"],\"checks\":[\"Initial repository inspection completed; P06 deliverables and test file are absent.\",\"Existing Core 0 context validation omits concept in merge comparisons, so P06 will enforce concept explicitly.\"],\"evidence\":[\"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/approved-plan.json\",\"scripts/core_semantics.py\",\"scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\",\"scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\",\"scripts/check_accounting_p04.py\"],\"issues\":[\"Repository does not expose a usable git worktree marker; manifests will record git provenance as unavailable and use content hashes.\"],\"next_actions\":[\"Write the P06 profile, fixture, and progress checkpoint.\",\"Implement context_chronology_v1.py, then tests and checker.\"],\"residuals\":[\"Full accounting validity and general mappings remain outside the bounded profile.\"],\"steps\":[\"Completed bounded interface inspection before editing.\"],\"summary\":\"Inspection confirms the approved slice is new and must supply its own context, chronology, uncertainty, grouping, tests, and provenance checker.\",\"verdict\":\"PLAN\"}"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06 docs/design/spec docs/design/fixtures\ncat > data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/progress.md <<'EOF'\n# P06 implementation progress\n\nInitial inspection completed against the approved plan and phase-entry inventory. The\nP06 deliverables and test module were absent. Existing Core 0 and P03/P04 helpers\nwere read as reference interfaces; their context merge and temporal arithmetic do\nnot establish the P06 criteria by themselves.\n\nPlanned edits: \"'`docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md`,\n`docs/design/fixtures/p06-context-chronology-cases-v1.json`,\n`scripts/context_chronology_v1.py`, `tests/test_accounting_p06.py`,\n`scripts/check_accounting_p06.py`, and the declared P06 outputs.\n\nSkeptical audit passed: the implementation will use independent exact-rational and\nfinite-membership oracles in tests; semantic rejection is required; query signatures\nwill bind grouping sufficiency; approximation requires a declared certificate; and\nsource-byte availability remains unresolved when evidence says so.\n\nNext checks: run the focused P06 suite, the P03/P04 regressions, then the provenance\nchecker with the supervisor approved-plan and pre-edit inventory paths. Repair any\nfailure before writing final result evidence.\nEOF\ncat > docs/design/spec/context-chronology-profile-v1.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Context, chronology, and resolution profile v1\n\nThis bounded profile implements P06 engineering behaviour for exact rational\nquantities, Gregorian half-open dates, finite populations, and nonnegative\nunhedged bullet debt. It is a versioned runtime contract, not an accounting\neligibility or forecast-validity claim.\n\n## Public operations\n\n\"'`Context` identifies concept, entity, perimeter and version, basis, measurement,\nunit/currency, calendar, dimensions, and gross/net status. `compatible_context`\nrequires all fields to match or an explicit dated `MappingRule`; parent/group,\nperimeter, basis, measurement, currency, calendar, dimension, and gross/net\nmismatches are rejected. Mapping cycles, expired rules, and unsupported conversion\nkinds fail with stable diagnostic codes.\n\n`check_partition` independently checks finite member sets. Members must be disjoint\nand cover the declared population, or an explicitly named residual must be present;\nan unknown residual cannot produce an exact total. Population and axis signatures\nprevent combining alternative classifications.\n\n`select_evidence` validates a supersession DAG and filters assertions by filing\navailability and optional ingestion cutoff before selecting `original`,\n`latest_available`, or `harmonised`. Date-only availability requires an explicit\nnamed timezone and `next_local_midnight` policy. Unknown retained-byte vintage is\nreturned as unresolved. Harmonisation preserves source IDs and transformation\nprovenance.\n\n`subtract_cumulative` computes an exact scalar flow only when concept, context,\ncalendar, start, nested exclusive ends, and revision compatibility agree. It\nrejects instant values and incompatible vintages; reviewed exceptions must name\nscope and evidence.\n\n`admit_uncertainty` supports exactly six categories: ExtractionReading,\nHistoricalFact, AccountingElection, MeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy, and\nFutureInnovation. It validates dependencies and category-specific fields. Unknown\ncategories, unsupported methods/treatments, invalid finite joint laws, and\nincompatible measures fail explicitly.\n\n`resolve_bullet_debt` retains constituents and validates a query signature over\ncontract, context, evidence view, horizon, scenario, requested outputs, and accrual\nconvention. Any changed signature requires fresh validation. The supported exact\ncase is fixed-rate unhedged bullet debt with no maturity crossing. The optional\nfixed-rate approximation requires nonnegative horizon, a declared tolerance, and a\ncertificate using the triangle inequality:\n`|sum(P_i r_i T)-sum(P_i) r* T| <= T sum(P_i |r_i-r*|)`.\n\n## Evidence and default audit\n\n| Choice | Provenance | Failure mode | Smallest diagnostic | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Exact `Fraction` arithmetic | Core 0 and P03 rational helpers | float rounding changes subtraction or bounds | independent Fraction oracle | reviewed bounded default |\n| Gregorian half-open dates | Core 0 temporal fixture | inclusive end or calendar mismatch | nested interval tests | reviewed bounded default |\n| Date-only next-local-midnight | approved P06 plan | UTC/local boundary selects wrong assertion | named-zone boundary test | explicit policy |\n| Finite partition populations | approved P06 plan | proof string hides overlap or omission | set enumeration | convenience test input |\n| Six uncertainty categories | P03 admission fields and approved plan | malformed evidence admitted | positive plus semantic negative per category | bounded support |\n| Bullet-debt grouping | P04 additive reference and approved plan | stale/query-insufficient grouping | query signature and constituent oracle | bounded hypothesis |\n| Approximation certificate | approved plan derivation | tolerance claimed without error bound | exact difference versus bound | optional reviewed path |\n\nSynthetic fixtures test structure only. P01 source records with\n`historical_byte_vintage=not_established_by_this_inventory` remain unresolved for\nhistorical byte selection. Passing this profile does not establish professional\naccounting treatment, empirical forecast validity, or human acceptance.\n\n## Criterion map\n\nMC02/MC05: context and partition checks; MC06/MC07: chronology and YTD revision\nselection; MC10: category admission; MC11/MC14: query-dependent grouping and\napproximation. Tests in `tests/test_accounting_p06.py` provide independent expected\nsets and arithmetic.\nEOF\ncat > docs/design/fixtures/p06-context-chronology-cases-v1.json <<'\"'EOF'\n{\n  \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"accdsl.p06.context-chronology-cases.v1\\\",\n  \\\"contexts\\\": {\n    \\\"usd_local\\\": {\\\"concept\\\":\\\"revenue\\\",\\\"entity\\\":\\\"Acme\\\",\\\"perimeter\\\":\\\"Acme\\\",\\\"perimeter_version\\\":\\\"2026\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"GAAP\\\",\\\"measurement\\\":\\\"historical_cost\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"currency\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"calendar\\\":\\\"gregorian\\\",\\\"dimensions\\\":{\\\"segment\\\":\\\"retail\\\"},\\\"gross_net\\\":\\\"gross\\\"},\n    \\\"usd_group\\\": {\\\"concept\\\":\\\"revenue\\\",\\\"entity\\\":\\\"Acme\\\",\\\"perimeter\\\":\\\"Group\\\",\\\"perimeter_version\\\":\\\"2026\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"GAAP\\\",\\\"measurement\\\":\\\"historical_cost\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"currency\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"calendar\\\":\\\"gregorian\\\",\\\"dimensions\\\":{\\\"segment\\\":\\\"retail\\\"},\\\"gross_net\\\":\\\"gross\\\"}\n  },\n  \\\"assertions\\\": [\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"h1-original\\\",\\\"concept\\\":\\\"sales\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"120\\\",\\\"period\\\":{\\\"start\\\":\\\"2025-01-01\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"2025-06-30\\\"},\\\"available\\\":\\\"2025-08-01\\\",\\\"ingested\\\":\\\"2025-08-02\\\",\\\"supersedes\\\":[],\\\"source\\\":\\\"fixture:original\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"h1-revised\\\",\\\"concept\\\":\\\"sales\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"110\\\",\\\"period\\\":{\\\"start\\\":\\\"2025-01-01\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"2025-06-30\\\"},\\\"available\\\":\\\"2026-02-01\\\",\\\"ingested\\\":\\\"2026-02-02\\\",\\\"supersedes\\\":[\\\"h1-original\\\"],\\\"source\\\":\\\"fixture:revision\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"fy25\\\",\\\"concept\\\":\\\"sales\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"260\\\",\\\"period\\\":{\\\"start\\\":\\\"2025-01-01\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"2025-12-31\\\"},\\\"available\\\":\\\"2026-02-01\\\",\\\"ingested\\\":\\\"2026-02-02\\\",\\\"supersedes\\\":[],\\\"source\\\":\\\"fixture:annual\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"expected\\\": {\\\"h2_from_revision\\\":\\\"150\\\", \\\"date_only_policy\\\":\\\"next_local_midnight\\\"}\n}\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
