s all fields to match or an explicit dated `MappingRule`; parent/group,\nperimeter, basis, measurement, currency, calendar, dimension, and gross/net\nmismatches are rejected. Mapping cycles, expired rules, and unsupported conversion\nkinds fail with stable diagnostic codes.\n\n`check_partition` independently checks finite member sets. Members must be disjoint\nand cover the declared population, or an explicitly named residual must be present;\nan unknown residual cannot produce an exact total. Population and axis signatures\nprevent combining alternative classifications.\n\n`select_evidence` validates a supersession DAG and filters assertions by filing\navailability and optional ingestion cutoff before selecting `original`,\n`latest_available`, or `harmonised`. Date-only availability requires an explicit\nnamed timezone and `next_local_midnight` policy. Unknown retained-byte vintage is\nreturned as unresolved. Harmonisation preserves source IDs and transformation\nprovenance.\n\n`subtract_cumulative` computes an exact scalar flow only when concept, context,\ncalendar, start, nested exclusive ends, and revision compatibility agree. It\nrejects instant values and incompatible vintages; reviewed exceptions must name\nscope and evidence.\n\n`admit_uncertainty` supports exactly six categories: ExtractionReading,\nHistoricalFact, AccountingElection, MeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy, and\nFutureInnovation. It validates dependencies and category-specific fields. Unknown\ncategories, unsupported methods/treatments, invalid finite joint laws, and\nincompatible measures fail explicitly.\n\n`resolve_bullet_debt` retains constituents and validates a query signature over\ncontract, context, evidence view, horizon, scenario, requested outputs, and accrual\nconvention. Any changed signature requires fresh validation. The supported exact\ncase is fixed-rate unhedged bullet debt with no maturity crossing. The optional\nfixed-rate approximation requires nonnegative horizon, a declared tolerance, and a\ncertificate using the triangle inequality:\n`|sum(P_i r_i T)-sum(P_i) r* T| <= T sum(P_i |r_i-r*|)`.\n\n## Evidence and default audit\n\n| Choice | Provenance | Failure mode | Smallest diagnostic | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Exact `Fraction` arithmetic | Core 0 and P03 rational helpers | float rounding changes subtraction or bounds | independent Fraction oracle | reviewed bounded default |\n| Gregorian half-open dates | Core 0 temporal fixture | inclusive end or calendar mismatch | nested interval tests | reviewed bounded default |\n| Date-only next-local-midnight | approved P06 plan | UTC/local boundary selects wrong assertion | named-zone boundary test | explicit policy |\n| Finite partition populations | approved P06 plan | proof string hides overlap or omission | set enumeration | convenience test input |\n| Six uncertainty categories | P03 admission fields and approved plan | malformed evidence admitted | positive plus semantic negative per category | bounded support |\n| Bullet-debt grouping | P04 additive reference and approved plan | stale/query-insufficient grouping | query signature and constituent oracle | bounded hypothesis |\n| Approximation certificate | approved plan derivation | tolerance claimed without error bound | exact difference versus bound | optional reviewed path |\n\nSynthetic fixtures test structure only. P01 source records with\n`historical_byte_vintage=not_established_by_this_inventory` remain unresolved for\nhistorical byte selection. Passing this profile does not establish professional\naccounting treatment, empirical forecast validity, or human acceptance.\n\n## Criterion map\n\nMC02/MC05: context and partition checks; MC06/MC07: chronology and YTD revision\nselection; MC10: category admission; MC11/MC14: query-dependent grouping and\napproximation. Tests in `tests/test_accounting_p06.py` provide independent expected\nsets and arithmetic.\nEOF\ncat > docs/design/fixtures/p06-context-chronology-cases-v1.json <<'\"'EOF'\n{\n  \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"accdsl.p06.context-chronology-cases.v1\\\",\n  \\\"contexts\\\": {\n    \\\"usd_local\\\": {\\\"concept\\\":\\\"revenue\\\",\\\"entity\\\":\\\"Acme\\\",\\\"perimeter\\\":\\\"Acme\\\",\\\"perimeter_version\\\":\\\"2026\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"GAAP\\\",\\\"measurement\\\":\\\"historical_cost\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"currency\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"calendar\\\":\\\"gregorian\\\",\\\"dimensions\\\":{\\\"segment\\\":\\\"retail\\\"},\\\"gross_net\\\":\\\"gross\\\"},\n    \\\"usd_group\\\": {\\\"concept\\\":\\\"revenue\\\",\\\"entity\\\":\\\"Acme\\\",\\\"perimeter\\\":\\\"Group\\\",\\\"perimeter_version\\\":\\\"2026\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"GAAP\\\",\\\"measurement\\\":\\\"historical_cost\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"currency\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"calendar\\\":\\\"gregorian\\\",\\\"dimensions\\\":{\\\"segment\\\":\\\"retail\\\"},\\\"gross_net\\\":\\\"gross\\\"}\n  },\n  \\\"assertions\\\": [\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"h1-original\\\",\\\"concept\\\":\\\"sales\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"120\\\",\\\"period\\\":{\\\"start\\\":\\\"2025-01-01\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"2025-06-30\\\"},\\\"available\\\":\\\"2025-08-01\\\",\\\"ingested\\\":\\\"2025-08-02\\\",\\\"supersedes\\\":[],\\\"source\\\":\\\"fixture:original\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"h1-revised\\\",\\\"concept\\\":\\\"sales\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"110\\\",\\\"period\\\":{\\\"start\\\":\\\"2025-01-01\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"2025-06-30\\\"},\\\"available\\\":\\\"2026-02-01\\\",\\\"ingested\\\":\\\"2026-02-02\\\",\\\"supersedes\\\":[\\\"h1-original\\\"],\\\"source\\\":\\\"fixture:revision\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"fy25\\\",\\\"concept\\\":\\\"sales\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"260\\\",\\\"period\\\":{\\\"start\\\":\\\"2025-01-01\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"2025-12-31\\\"},\\\"available\\\":\\\"2026-02-01\\\",\\\"ingested\\\":\\\"2026-02-02\\\",\\\"supersedes\\\":[],\\\"source\\\":\\\"fixture:annual\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"expected\\\": {\\\"h2_from_revision\\\":\\\"150\\\", \\\"date_only_policy\\\":\\\"next_local_midnight\\\"}\n}\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > scripts/context_chronology_v1.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Bounded P06 context, chronology, uncertainty and resolution runtime.\n\nThe profile is intentionally explicit: it uses exact \"'``Fraction`` arithmetic,\nGregorian half-open periods, finite populations, and a fixed-rate unhedged bullet\ndebt resolver.  Every rejection has a stable ``P06Error.code``.  This module\nchecks structural and computational contracts; it does not certify accounting\neligibility or the truth of retained source evidence.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import date, datetime, time, timedelta, timezone\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom types import MappingProxyType\nfrom typing import Any, Iterable, Mapping, Sequence\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo, ZoneInfoNotFoundError\n\n\nclass P06Error(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"A rejected P06 operation with a stable diagnostic code.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, code: str, message: str, *, location: str = \"\"):\n        self.code, self.location, self.message = code, location, message\n        suffix = f\" at {location}\" if location else \"\"\n        super().__init__(f\"{code}{suffix}: {message}\")\n\n\ndef fail(code: str, message: str, location: str = \"\") -> None:\n    raise P06Error(code, message, location=location)\n\n\ndef _fraction(value: Any, where: str = \"value\") -> Fraction:\n    if isinstance(value, Fraction):\n        return value\n    if isinstance(value, bool):\n        fail(\"INVALID_RATIONAL\", \"boolean is not a scalar\", where)\n    try:\n        if isinstance(value, int):\n            return Fraction(value)\n        if isinstance(value, str):\n            return Fraction(value)\n        if isinstance(value, float):\n            # Floats are rejected to keep exactness explicit.\n            fail(\"INEXACT_RATIONAL\", \"float input is not accepted\", where)\n        if isinstance(value, Mapping) and set(value) == {\"n\", \"d\"}:\n            q = Fraction(int(value[\"n\"]), int(value[\"d\"]))\n            if int(value[\"d\"]) <= 0:\n                fail(\"INVALID_RATIONAL\", \"denominator must be positive\", where)\n            if {\"n\": str(q.numerator), \"d\": str(q.denominator)} != {\n                \"n\": str(value[\"n\"]), \"d\": str(value[\"d\"])\n            }:\n                fail(\"NONCANONICAL_RATIONAL\", \"fraction must be reduced\", where)\n            return q\n    except (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError) as exc:\n        fail(\"INVALID_RATIONAL\", str(exc), where)\n    fail(\"INVALID_RATIONAL\", \"expected an integer or canonical rational\", where)\n\n\ndef _iso_date(value: Any, where: str) -> date:\n    if not isinstance(value, str):\n        fail(\"INVALID_DATE\", \"date must be YYYY-MM-DD\", where)\n    try:\n        parsed = date.fromisoformat(value)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        fail(\"INVALID_DATE\", str(exc), where)\n    if parsed.isoformat() != value:\n        fail(\"INVALID_DATE\", \"noncanonical ISO date\", where)\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _instant(value: Any, where: str) -> datetime:\n    if not isinstance(value, str):\n        fail(\"INVALID_TIMESTAMP\", \"timestamp must be an ISO string\", where)\n    try:\n        parsed = datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\"))\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        fail(\"INVALID_TIMESTAMP\", str(exc), where)\n    if parsed.tzinfo is None:\n        fail(\"MISSING_TIMEZONE\", \"timestamp requires an explicit timezone\", where)\n    return parsed\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Context:\n    concept: str\n    entity: str\n    perimeter: str\n    perimeter_version: str\n    basis: str\n    measurement: str\n    unit: str\n    currency: str\n    calendar: str\n    dimensions: tuple[tuple[str, str], ...] = ()\n    gross_net: str = \"gross\"\n    parent: str | None = None\n    group: str | None = None\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> \"Context\":\n        required = (\"concept\", \"entity\", \"perimeter\", \"perimeter_version\", \"basis\",\n                    \"measurement\", \"unit\", \"currency\", \"calendar\", \"dimensions\", \"gross_net\")\n        for key in required:\n            if key not in row:\n                fail(\"MISSING_CONTEXT_FIELD\", f\"missing {key}\", \"context\")\n        dims = row[\"dimensions\"]\n        if not isinstance(dims, Mapping):\n            fail(\"INVALID_DIMENSIONS\", \"dimensions must be an object\", \"context.dimensions\")\n        if any(not isinstance(k, str) or not isinstance(v, str) for k, v in dims.items()):\n            fail(\"INVALID_DIMENSIONS\", \"dimension keys and values must be strings\", \"context.dimensions\")\n        if row[\"gross_net\"] not in {\"gross\", \"net\"}:\n            fail(\"INVALID_GROSS_NET\", \"gross_net must be gross or net\", \"context.gross_net\")\n        return cls(*(str(row[k]) for k in required[:9]),\n                   tuple(sorted((str(k), str(v)) for k, v in dims.items())),\n                   str(row[\"gross_net\"]), row.get(\"parent\"), row.get(\"group\"))\n\n    def as_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        return {\n            \"concept\": self.concept, \"entity\": self.entity, \"perimeter\": self.perimeter,\n            \"perimeter_version\": self.perimeter_version, \"basis\": self.basis,\n            \"measurement\": self.measurement, \"unit\": self.unit, \"currency\": self.currency,\n            \"calendar\": self.calendar, \"dimensions\": dict(self.dimensions),\n            \"gross_net\": self.gross_net, \"parent\": self.parent, \"group\": self.group,\n        }\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass MappingRule:\n    source_concept: str\n    target_concept: str\n    kind: str = \"equivalent\"\n    source_context: str | None = None\n    target_context: str | None = None\n    effective_start: date | None = None\n    effective_end: date | None = None\n    conversion: str | None = None\n    provenance: tuple[str, ...] = ()\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> \"MappingRule\":\n        if not row.get(\"provenance\"):\n            fail(\"MAPPING_PROVENANCE_REQUIRED\", \"mapping provenance is required\", \"mapping\")\n        start = _iso_date(row[\"effective_start\"], \"mapping.effective_start\") if row.get(\"effective_start\") else None\n        end = _iso_date(row[\"effective_end\"], \"mapping.effective_end\") if row.get(\"effective_end\") else None\n        if start and end and end <= start:\n            fail(\"INVALID_MAPPING_WINDOW\", \"effective end must follow start\", \"mapping\")\n        kind = row.get(\"kind\", \"equivalent\")\n        if kind not in {\"equivalent\", \"component\", \"reclassification\"}:\n            fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_MAPPING\", f\"unsupported mapping kind {kind}\", \"mapping\")\n        return cls(str(row[\"source_concept\"]), str(row[\"target_concept\"]), kind,\n                   row.get(\"source_context\"), row.get(\"target_context\"), start, end,\n                   row.get(\"conversion\"), tuple(str(x) for x in row[\"provenance\"]))\n\n    def active(self, when: date | None) -> bool:\n        if when is None:\n            return self.effective_start is None and self.effective_end is None\n        return ((self.effective_start is None or when >= self.effective_start) and\n                (self.effective_end is None or when < self.effective_end))\n\n\ndef _context_mismatch(a: Context, b: Context) -> tuple[str, str] | None:\n    fields = (\"entity\", \"perimeter\", \"perimeter_version\", \"basis\", \"measurement\", \"unit\",\n              \"currency\", \"calendar\", \"dimensions\", \"gross_net\", \"parent\", \"group\")\n    for field_name in fields:\n        if getattr(a, field_name) != getattr(b, field_name):\n            return field_name, getattr(a, field_name).__repr__() + \" != \" + getattr(b, field_name).__repr__()\n    if a.concept != b.concept:\n        return \"concept\", repr(a.concept) + \" != \" + repr(b.concept)\n    return None\n\n\ndef _check_mapping_graph(rules: Sequence[MappingRule]) -> None:\n    graph: dict[str, set[str]] = {}\n    for rule in rules:\n        graph.setdefault(rule.source_concept, set()).add(rule.target_concept)\n    state: dict[str, int] = {}\n    def visit(node: str) -> None:\n        state[node] = 1\n        for nxt in graph.get(node, ()):\n            if state.get(nxt) == 1:\n                fail(\"MAPPING_CYCLE\", \"mapping graph contains a cycle\", node)\n            if state.get(nxt) != 2:\n                visit(nxt)\n        state[node] = 2\n    for node in graph:\n        if state.get(node, 0) == 0:\n            visit(node)\n\n\ndef compatible_context(source: Context | Mapping[str, Any], target: Context | Mapping[str, Any],\n                       rules: Sequence[MappingRule | Mapping[str, Any]] = (),\n                       *, at: str | date | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Return a mapping witness or reject a context mismatch.\"\"\"\n    a = source if isinstance(source, Context) else Context.from_dict(source)\n    b = target if isinstance(target, Context) else Context.from_dict(target)\n    when = _iso_date(at, \"mapping.at\") if isinstance(at, str) else at\n    parsed = [x if isinstance(x, MappingRule) else MappingRule.from_dict(x) for x in rules]\n    _check_mapping_graph(parsed)\n    mismatch = _context_mismatch(a, b)\n    if mismatch is None:\n        return {\"status\": \"compatible\", \"kind\": \"identity\", \"source\": a.as_dict(), \"target\": b.as_dict()}\n    field_name, detail = mismatch\n    if field_name == \"concept\":\n        eligible = [r for r in parsed if r.source_concept == a.concept and r.target_concept == b.concept and r.active(when)]\n        if not eligible:\n            fail(\"CONTEXT_MISMATCH\", f\"concept mismatch {detail} requires an explicit active mapping\", field_name)\n        rule = eligible[0]\n        if rule.kind == \"equivalent\" and (rule.conversion or \"\") not in {\"\", \"none\"}:\n            fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_MEASUREMENT_CONVERSION\", \"equivalent mapping cannot convert measurements\", field_name)\n        if rule.source_context and rule.source_context != a.entity:\n            fail(\"MAPPING_SOURCE_CONTEXT_MISMATCH\", \"mapping source context does not match\", field_name)\n        if rule.target_context and rule.target_context != b.entity:\n            fail(\"MAPPING_TARGET_CONTEXT_MISMATCH\", \"mapping target context does not match\", field_name)\n        return {\"status\": \"compatible\", \"kind\": rule.kind, \"source\": a.as_dict(), \"target\": b.as_dict(),\n                \"provenance\": list(rule.provenance)}\n    codes = {\"perimeter\": \"PARENT_GROUP_MISMATCH\", \"perimeter_version\": \"PERIMETER_VERSION_MISMATCH\",\n             \"basis\": \"BASIS_MISMATCH\", \"measurement\": \"MEASUREMENT_MISMATCH\", \"currency\": \"CURRENCY_MISMATCH\",\n             \"calendar\": \"CALENDAR_MISMATCH\", \"gross_net\": \"GROSS_NET_MISMATCH\", \"dimensions\": \"DIMENSION_MISMATCH\",\n             \"entity\": \"ENTITY_MISMATCH\", \"unit\": \"UNIT_MISMATCH\", \"parent\": \"PARENT_GROUP_MISMATCH\", \"group\": \"PARENT_GROUP_MISMATCH\"}\n    fail(codes.get(field_name, \"CONTEXT_MISMATCH\"), f\"context field mismatch: {detail}\", field_name)\n\n\ndef map_context(source: Context | Mapping[str, Any], target: Context | Mapping[str, Any],\n                rules: Sequence[MappingRule | Mapping[str, Any]] = (), *, at: str | date | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return compatible_context(source, target, rules, at=at)\n\n\ndef check_partition(population: Iterable[str], members: Mapping[str, Iterable[str]], *,\n                    residual: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None, axis: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n    pop = list(population)\n    if len(pop) != len(set(pop)):\n        fail(\"DUPLICATE_POPULATION\", \"population identifiers must be unique\", axis)\n    universe = set(pop)\n    seen: dict[str, str] = {}\n    normalized: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n    for label, values in members.items():\n        vals = list(values)\n        if len(vals) != len(set(vals)):\n            fail(\"DUPLICATE_MEMBER\", f\"member repeated in {label}\", axis)\n        unknown = set(vals) - universe\n        if unknown:\n            fail(\"UNKNOWN_MEMBER\", f\"members outside population: {sorted(unknown)}\", axis)\n        for value in vals:\n            if value in seen:\n                fail(\"OVERLAPPING_PARTITION\", f\"{value} occurs in {seen[value]} and {label}\", axis)\n            seen[value] = label\n        normalized[label] = vals\n    missing = universe - set(seen)\n    if missing:\n        if not residual:\n            fail(\"INCOMPLETE_PARTITION\", f\"uncovered members: {sorted(missing)}\", axis)\n        residual_values = set(residual.get(\"members\", ()))\n        if residual_values != missing:\n            fail(\"INVALID_RESIDUAL\", \"residual must identify exactly uncovered members\", axis)\n        if not residual.get(\"known\", False):\n            fail(\"UNKNOWN_RESIDUAL\", \"unknown residual cannot yield an exact total\", axis)\n    if residual and set(residual.get(\"members\", ())) & set(seen):\n        fail(\"OVERLAPPING_PARTITION\", \"residual overlaps a named member\", axis)\n    return {\"status\": \"partitioned\", \"axis\": axis, \"population\": pop, \"members\": normalized,\n            \"residual\": dict(residual) if residual else None, \"covered\": len(seen), \"complete\": not missing}\n\n\ndef _availability(value: Any, *, timezone_name: str | None, date_only_policy: str | None, where: str) -> datetime:\n    if isinstance(value, datetime):\n        if value.tzinfo is None:\n            fail(\"MISSING_TIMEZONE\", \"timestamp requires timezone\", where)\n        return value\n    if isinstance(value, date):\n        value = value.isoformat()\n    if not isinstance(value, str):\n        fail(\"INVALID_AVAILABILITY\", \"availability must be date or timestamp\", where)\n    if \"T\" in value or \" \" in value:\n        return _instant(value, where)\n    d = _iso_date(value, where)\n    if date_only_policy != \"next_local_midnight\":\n        fail(\"DATE_ONLY_POLICY_REQUIRED\", \"date-only availability requires next_local_midnight\", where)\n    if not timezone_name:\n        fail(\"TIMEZONE_REQUIRED\", \"named timezone required for date-only availability\", where)\n    try:\n        zone = ZoneInfo(timezone_name)\n    except ZoneInfoNotFoundError:\n        fail(\"UNKNOWN_TIMEZONE\", timezone_name, where)\n    return datetime.combine(d + timedelta(days=1), time.min, zone)\n\n\ndef _validate_assertions(assertions: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]]) -> dict[str, Mapping[str, Any]]:\n    rows = {str(a.get(\"id\")): a for a in assertions}\n    if len(rows) != len(assertions) or None in rows:\n        fail(\"DUPLICATE_ASSERTION\", \"assertion identifiers must be unique\", \"assertions\")\n    for row in assertions:\n        if not row.get(\"source\"):\n            fail(\"MISSING_SOURCE\", \"assertion source is required\", str(row.get(\"id\")))\n        for parent in row.get(\"supersedes\", []):\n            if parent not in rows:\n                fail(\"DANGLING_SUPERSESSION\", f\"unknown superseded assertion {parent}\", str(row.get(\"id\")))\n            if parent == row[\"id\"]:\n                fail(\"SUPERSESSION_CYCLE\", \"assertion cannot supersede itself\", str(row[\"id\"]))\n    state: dict[str, int] = {}\n    def visit(key: str) -> None:\n        state[key] = 1\n        for parent in rows[key].get(\"supersedes\", []):\n            if state.get(parent) == 1:\n                fail(\"SUPERSESSION_CYCLE\", \"supersession graph contains a cycle\", key)\n            if state.get(parent) != 2:\n                visit(parent)\n        state[key] = 2\n    for key in rows:\n        if state.get(key, 0) == 0:\n            visit(key)\n    return rows\n\n\ndef select_evidence(assertions: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]], cutoff: str | datetime | date, *,\n                    mode: str = \"latest_available\", system_as_of: str | datetime | date | None = None,\n                    timezone_name: str | None = None, date_only_policy: str | None = None,\n                    harmonisations: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]] = ()) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    rows = _validate_assertions(assertions)\n    if mode not in {\"original\", \"latest_available\", \"harmonised\"}:\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_EVIDENCE_VIEW\", mode, \"mode\")\n    if isinstance(cutoff, datetime):\n        cut = cutoff if cutoff.tzinfo else fail(\"MISSING_TIMEZONE\", \"cutoff requires timezone\", \"cutoff\")\n    else:\n        cut = _availability(cutoff, timezone_name=timezone_name, date_only_policy=date_only_policy, where=\"cutoff\")\n    asof = None\n    if system_as_of is not None:\n        asof = system_as_of if isinstance(system_as_of, datetime) else _availability(system_as_of, timezone_name=timezone_name, date_only_policy=date_only_policy, where=\"system_as_of\")\n    eligible = []\n    unresolved = []\n    for row in assertions:\n        try:\n            available = _availability(row[\"available\"], timezone_name=timezone_name, date_only_policy=date_only_policy, where=f\"{row['\"'id']}.available\\\")\n            ingested = _availability(row.get(\\\"ingested\\\", row[\\\"available\\\"]), timezone_name=timezone_name, date_only_policy=date_only_policy, where=f\\\"{row['id']}.ingested\\\")\n        except P06Error:\n            raise\n        if available <= cut and (asof is None or ingested <= asof):\n            eligible.append(row)\n        if row.get(\\\"historical_byte_vintage\\\") in {None, \\\"not_established_by_this_inventory\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"}:\n            unresolved.append({\\\"id\\\": row[\\\"id\\\"], \\\"reason\\\": \\\"historical_byte_vintage_unestablished\\\"})\n    eligible_ids = {x[\\\"id\\\"] for x in eligible}\n    if mode == \\\"original\\\":\n        selected = [x for x in eligible if not any(parent in eligible_ids for parent in x.get(\\\"supersedes\\\", []))]\n        # Roots are the first available assertions in a lineage: remove rows that supersede them.\n        selected = [x for x in selected if not x.get(\\\"supersedes\\\")]\n    else:\n        superseded = {parent for x in eligible for parent in x.get(\\\"supersedes\\\", [])}\n        selected = [x for x in eligible if x[\\\"id\\\"] not in superseded]\n    transformations = []\n    if mode == \\\"harmonised\\\":\n        for h in harmonisations:\n            source = h.get(\\\"source_id\\\")\n            if source not in {x[\\\"id\\\"] for x in selected}:\n                continue\n            if h.get(\\\"review_decision\\\") \"'!= \"Accept\" or not h.get(\"provenance\"):\n                fail(\"HARMONISATION_NOT_REVIEWED\", \"harmonisation requires accepted review and provenance\", str(source))\n            if h.get(\"changes_basis\") or h.get(\"changes_measurement\"):\n                fail(\"HARMONISATION_CONTEXT_CHANGE\", \"harmonisation cannot replace basis or measurement\", str(source))\n            transformations.append({\"source_id\": source, \"target_id\": h.get(\"target_id\", source), \"provenance\": list(h[\"provenance\"])})\n    return {\"mode\": mode, \"cutoff\": str(cutoff), \"selected\": [dict(x) for x in selected],\n            \"selected_ids\": [x[\"id\"] for x in selected], \"eligible_ids\": sorted(eligible_ids),\n            \"unresolved\": unresolved, \"transformations\": transformations}\n\n\ndef _row_context(row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return json.dumps(row.get(\"context\", {}), sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n\n\ndef subtract_cumulative(total: Mapping[str, Any], earlier: Mapping[str, Any], *,\n                        revision_compatibility: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    for label, row in ((\"total\", total), (\"earlier\", earlier)):\n        if row.get(\"kind\") != \"cumulative\":\n            fail(\"YTD_REQUIRES_CUMULATIVE\", f\"{label} must be cumulative\", label)\n        if row.get(\"period\", {}).get(\"end\") is None:\n            fail(\"INVALID_PERIOD\", \"cumulative period requires exclusive end\", label)\n    if total.get(\"concept\") != earlier.get(\"concept\"):\n        fail(\"CONCEPT_MISMATCH\", \"flow concepts differ\", \"ytd\")\n    if _row_context(total) != _row_context(earlier):\n        fail(\"CONTEXT_MISMATCH\", \"cumulative contexts differ\", \"ytd\")\n    if total.get(\"calendar\") != earlier.get(\"calendar\"):\n        fail(\"CALENDAR_MISMATCH\", \"calendars differ\", \"ytd\")\n    tp, ep = total[\"period\"], earlier[\"period\"]\n    if tp.get(\"start\") != ep.get(\"start\"):\n        fail(\"PERIOD_START_MISMATCH\", \"cumulative periods must share a start\", \"ytd\")\n    tend, eend = _iso_date(tp[\"end\"], \"total.period.end\"), _iso_date(ep[\"end\"], \"earlier.period.end\")\n    if eend >= tend:\n        fail(\"NONNESTED_PERIOD\", \"earlier period must end before total\", \"ytd\")\n    tstart = _iso_date(tp[\"start\"], \"total.period.start\")\n    if _iso_date(ep[\"start\"], \"earlier.period.start\") != tstart:\n        fail(\"PERIOD_START_MISMATCH\", \"period starts differ\", \"ytd\")\n    tr = total.get(\"revision_id\"); er = earlier.get(\"revision_id\")\n    if tr != er:\n        allowed = revision_compatibility and revision_compatibility.get(\"accepted\")\n        if not allowed or not revision_compatibility.get(\"scope\") or not revision_compatibility.get(\"evidence\"):\n            fail(\"REVISION_INCOMPATIBLE\", \"subtraction requires a common revision or reviewed scoped exception\", \"ytd\")\n    amount = _fraction(total[\"amount\"], \"total.amount\") - _fraction(earlier[\"amount\"], \"earlier.amount\")\n    return {\"kind\": \"flow\", \"amount\": amount, \"period\": {\"start\": ep[\"end\"], \"end\": tp[\"end\"]},\n            \"concept\": total[\"concept\"], \"context\": total.get(\"context\"), \"calendar\": total[\"calendar\"],\n            \"provenance\": {\"operation\": \"cumulative_subtraction\", \"total_id\": total.get(\"id\"), \"earlier_id\": earlier.get(\"id\"),\n                           \"revision_id\": tr or er}}\n\n\n_SUPPORTED_MEASUREMENT_METHODS = {\"direct\", \"discounted_cash_flow\", \"observable_input\"}\n_SUPPORTED_MEASURES = {\"real_world\", \"pricing\"}\n\n\ndef _validate_joint_law(law: Any, where: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    atoms = law.get(\"atoms\") if isinstance(law, Mapping) else law\n    if not isinstance(atoms, list) or not atoms:\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"finite joint law needs atoms\", where)\n    ids = [a.get(\"id\") for a in atoms]\n    if any(not isinstance(x, str) for x in ids) or len(ids) != len(set(ids)):\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"atom IDs must be distinct\", where)\n    hypotheses = [a.get(\"hypothesis\") for a in atoms]\n    if any(not isinstance(h, Mapping) or not h for h in hypotheses):\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"complete scalar hypotheses are required\", where)\n    if len({json.dumps(h, sort_keys=True) for h in hypotheses}) != len(hypotheses):\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"joint hypotheses overlap\", where)\n    weights = [_fraction(a.get(\"weight\"), where) for a in atoms]\n    if any(w < 0 for w in weights) or sum(weights, Fraction()) != 1:\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"weights must be nonnegative and sum to one\", where)\n    return [dict(a) for a in atoms]\n\n\ndef admit_uncertainty(record: Mapping[str, Any], *, known_records: Mapping[str, Mapping[str, Any]] | None = None,\n                      available_information: Iterable[str] = ()) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    kind = record.get(\"kind\")\n    fields = {\n        \"ExtractionReading\": (\"source\", \"locator\", \"review_decision\"),\n        \"HistoricalFact\": (\"evidence\", \"reason\"),\n        \"AccountingElection\": (\"package\", \"permitted_treatments\", \"election\", \"effective_date\", \"eligibility_evidence\"),\n        \"MeasurementEstimate\": (\"method\", \"measurement_date\", \"inputs\"),\n        \"BehaviourPolicy\": (\"policy\", \"information_set\", \"decision_time\"),\n        \"FutureInnovation\": (\"driver\", \"future_period\", \"scenario\", \"joint_law\", \"measure\"),\n    }\n    if kind not in fields:\n        fail(\"UNKNOWN_UNCERTAINTY_CATEGORY\", f\"unsupported category {kind!r}\", \"kind\")\n    for key in (\"id\", \"scope\", \"provenance\", \"dependencies\") + fields[kind]:\n        if key not in record or (key != \"dependencies\" and not record[key]):\n            fail(\"MISSING_ADMISSION_FIELD\", f\"missing admission field {key}\", str(record.get(\"id\", \"\")))\n    if not isinstance(record[\"provenance\"], list) or not isinstance(record[\"dependencies\"], list):\n        fail(\"INVALID_ADMISSION_LIST\", \"provenance and dependencies must be lists\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    known_records = known_records or {}\n    for dep in record[\"dependencies\"]:\n        if dep not in known_records:\n            fail(\"DANGLING_DEPENDENCY\", f\"unknown dependency {dep}\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"ExtractionReading\" and record[\"review_decision\"] != \"Accept\":\n        fail(\"READING_NOT_ACCEPTED\", \"reading requires accepted review\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"AccountingElection\" and record[\"election\"] not in record[\"permitted_treatments\"]:\n        fail(\"TREATMENT_NOT_PERMITTED\", \"election is outside package permissions\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"MeasurementEstimate\":\n        if record[\"method\"] not in _SUPPORTED_MEASUREMENT_METHODS:\n            fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_ESTIMATION_METHOD\", record[\"method\"], str(record[\"id\"]))\n        if not isinstance(record[\"inputs\"], Mapping) or any(v is None for v in record[\"inputs\"].values()):\n            fail(\"MISSING_ESTIMATE_INPUT\", \"measurement inputs must be available\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"BehaviourPolicy\":\n        if not isinstance(record[\"information_set\"], list):\n            fail(\"INVALID_INFORMATION_SET\", \"information_set must be a list\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n        if any(str(x).startswith(\"future_realised:\") for x in record[\"information_set\"]):\n            fail(\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\", \"future realised outcome is unavailable at decision time\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"FutureInnovation\":\n        if record[\"measure\"] not in _SUPPORTED_MEASURES:\n            fail(\"INCOMPATIBLE_PROBABILITY_MEASURE\", \"measure must be real_world or pricing\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n        _validate_joint_law(record[\"joint_law\"], str(record[\"id\"]))\n    return dict(record)\n\n\ndef guard_information_view(view: Mapping[str, Any], *, event_time: str | date, request: str = \"exogenous_stress\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n    if request in {\"observational_conditioning\", \"structural_intervention\"}:\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_INFORMATION_OPERATION\", request, \"information_view\")\n    visible = set(view.get(\"visible\", ()))\n    future_stress = set(view.get(\"future_announced\", ()))\n    hidden = set(view.get(\"future_realised\", ()))\n    if hidden & visible:\n        fail(\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\", \"future realised outcomes cannot be visible\", \"information_view\")\n    if not view.get(\"measure_id\"):\n        fail(\"MISSING_PROBABILITY_MEASURE\", \"information view needs an explicit measure\", \"information_view\")\n    if view.get(\"pricing_measure_id\") and view[\"pricing_measure_id\"] == view[\"measure_id\"]:\n        fail(\"INCOMPATIBLE_PROBABILITY_MEASURE\", \"real-world and pricing measures must be distinct\", \"information_view\")\n    return {\"status\": \"accepted\", \"event_time\": str(event_time), \"visible\": sorted(visible),\n            \"future_announced\": sorted(future_stress), \"future_realised_hidden\": sorted(hidden),\n            \"measure_id\": view[\"measure_id\"], \"selection_changes_history\": False}\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass DebtConstituent:\n    id: str\n    principal: Fraction\n    rate: Fraction\n    maturity: Fraction\n    reset: str = \"fixed\"\n    hedge: str = \"unhedged\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> \"DebtConstituent\":\n        principal = _fraction(row.get(\"principal\"), f\"{row.get('\"'id')}.principal\\\")\n        if principal < 0:\n            fail(\\\"NEGATIVE_PRINCIPAL\\\", \\\"principal must be nonnegative\\\", str(row.get(\\\"id\\\")))\n        return cls(str(row[\\\"id\\\"]), principal, _fraction(row.get(\\\"rate\\\"), f\\\"{row.get('id')}.rate\\\"),\n                   _fraction(row.get(\\\"maturity\\\"), f\\\"{row.get('id')}.maturity\\\"), str(row.get(\\\"reset\\\", \\\"fixed\\\")), str(row.get(\\\"hedge\\\", \\\"unhedged\\\")))\n\n\ndef _query_signature(query: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(query, sort_keys=True, default=str, separators=(\\\",\\\", \\\":\\\")).encode()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef interest_certificate(constituents: Sequence[DebtConstituent], target_rate: Fraction | str | int,\n                         horizon: Fraction | str | int) -> dict[str, Fraction]:\n    T = _fraction(horizon, \\\"horizon\\\")\n    if T < 0:\n        fail(\\\"INVALID_HORIZON\\\", \\\"horizon must be nonnegative\\\", \\\"horizon\\\")\n    rstar = _fraction(target_rate, \\\"target_rate\\\")\n    exact = sum((c.principal * c.rate * T for c in constituents), Fraction())\n    approx = sum((c.principal * rstar * T for c in constituents), Fraction())\n    bound = T * sum((c.principal * abs(c.rate - rstar) for c in constituents), Fraction())\n    difference = abs(exact - approx)\n    if difference > bound:\n        fail(\\\"INVALID_APPROXIMATION_CERTIFICATE\\\", \\\"triangle-inequality bound is violated\\\", \\\"approximation\\\")\n    return {\\\"exact\\\": exact, \\\"approximate\\\": approx, \\\"error\\\": difference, \\\"bound\\\": bound}\n\n\ndef resolve_bullet_debt(constituents: Sequence[DebtConstituent | Mapping[str, Any]], query: Mapping[str, Any], *,\n                       previous: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None,\n                       approximation: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    rows = [x if isinstance(x, DebtConstituent) else DebtConstituent.from_dict(x) for x in constituents]\n    if not rows:\n        fail(\\\"EMPTY_DEBT_SET\\\", \\\"at least one constituent is required\\\", \\\"debt\\\")\n    required = (\\\"contract\\\", \\\"context\\\", \\\"evidence_view\\\", \\\"horizon\\\", \\\"scenario\\\", \\\"requested_outputs\\\", \\\"accrual_convention\\\", \\\"group_by\\\")\n    for key in required:\n        if key not in query:\n            fail(\\\"MISSING_QUERY_FIELD\\\", f\\\"missing {key}\\\", \\\"query\\\")\n    signature = _query_signature(query)\n    if previous is not None and previous.get(\\\"query_signature\\\") \"'!= signature:\n        fail(\"STALE_RESULT\", \"query changed; grouping sufficiency must be revalidated\", \"query\")\n    horizon = _fraction(query[\"horizon\"], \"query.horizon\")\n    if horizon < 0:\n        fail(\"INVALID_HORIZON\", \"horizon must be nonnegative\", \"query.horizon\")\n    if query[\"scenario\"] not in {\"base\", \"announced_stress\"}:\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_SCENARIO\", str(query[\"scenario\"]), \"query.scenario\")\n    if query[\"accrual_convention\"] != \"simple_actual_fraction\":\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_ACCRUAL\", str(query[\"accrual_convention\"]), \"query.accrual_convention\")\n    if not isinstance(query[\"requested_outputs\"], list) or not query[\"requested_outputs\"]:\n        fail(\"MISSING_OUTPUT_REQUEST\", \"requested_outputs must be nonempty\", \"query\")\n    dimensions = (\"rate\", \"maturity\", \"reset\", \"hedge\")\n    group_by = set(query[\"group_by\"])\n    if not group_by <= set(dimensions):\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_GROUP_DIMENSION\", \"group_by contains unsupported dimension\", \"query.group_by\")\n    for dim in dimensions:\n        values = {getattr(c, dim) for c in rows}\n        if len(values) > 1 and dim not in group_by:\n            fail(\"GROUPING_INSUFFICIENT\", f\"dimension {dim} varies but is not grouped\", \"query.group_by\")\n    for c in rows:\n        if c.hedge != \"unhedged\":\n            fail(\"HEDGED_DEBT_UNSUPPORTED\", \"only unhedged debt is supported\", c.id)\n        if c.reset != \"fixed\":\n            fail(\"RESET_UNSUPPORTED\", \"only fixed reset is supported\", c.id)\n        if c.maturity < horizon:\n            fail(\"MATURITY_CROSSING\", \"maturity crosses the requested horizon\", c.id)\n    groups: dict[tuple[Any, ...], list[DebtConstituent]] = {}\n    for c in rows:\n        key = tuple(getattr(c, dim) if dim in group_by else \"homogeneous\" for dim in dimensions)\n        groups.setdefault(key, []).append(c)\n    output: dict[str, Any] = {}\n    if \"interest\" in query[\"requested_outputs\"]:\n        output[\"interest\"] = sum((c.principal * c.rate * horizon for c in rows), Fraction())\n    if \"principal\" in query[\"requested_outputs\"]:\n        output[\"principal\"] = sum((c.principal for c in rows), Fraction())\n    result = {\"status\": \"resolved\", \"query_signature\": signature,\n              \"query\": json.loads(json.dumps(query, default=str)), \"groups\": [\n                  {\"key\": [str(x) for x in key], \"constituent_ids\": [c.id for c in members],\n                   \"principal\": sum((c.principal for c in members), Fraction()),\n                   \"interest\": sum((c.principal * c.rate * horizon for c in members), Fraction())}\n                  for key, members in groups.items()],\n              \"outputs\": output, \"constituent_ids\": [c.id for c in rows], \"fresh\": True}\n    if approximation is not None:\n        if not approximation.get(\"scope\") or approximation.get(\"scope\") != \"fixed_rate_interest\" or not approximation.get(\"evidence\"):\n            fail(\"APPROXIMATION_EVIDENCE_REQUIRED\", \"declared scope and evidence are required\", \"approximation\")\n        cert = interest_certificate(rows, approximation.get(\"target_rate\"), horizon)\n        tolerance = _fraction(approximation.get(\"tolerance\"), \"approximation.tolerance\")\n        declared = _fraction(approximation.get(\"error_bound\"), \"approximation.error_bound\")\n        if tolerance < 0 or declared < cert[\"error\"] or declared > tolerance or declared < cert[\"bound\"]:\n            fail(\"APPROXIMATION_BOUND_INVALID\", \"declared bound must cover exact error and certificate within tolerance\", \"approximation\")\n        result[\"approximation\"] = {k: str(v) for k, v in cert.items()} | {\"tolerance\": str(tolerance), \"declared_error_bound\": str(declared)}\n    return result\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass P06Engine:\n    contexts: dict[str, Context] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    mappings: list[MappingRule] = field(default_factory=list)\n    assertions: list[dict[str, Any]] = field(default_factory=list)\n    uncertainty: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    current_results: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    preserved_results: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = field(default_factory=dict)\n\n    def add_context(self, identifier: str, context: Context | Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n        if identifier in self.contexts:\n            fail(\"DUPLICATE_CONTEXT\", identifier, identifier)\n        self.contexts[identifier] = context if isinstance(context, Context) else Context.from_dict(context)\n\n    def add_mapping(self, rule: MappingRule | Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n        self.mappings.append(rule if isinstance(rule, MappingRule) else MappingRule.from_dict(rule))\n        _check_mapping_graph(self.mappings)\n\n    def add_assertion(self, row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n        self.assertions.append(dict(row))\n        _validate_assertions(self.assertions)\n\n    def revise(self, assertion_id: str, replacement: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n        rows = {x[\"id\"]: x for x in self.assertions}\n        if assertion_id not in rows:\n            fail(\"UNKNOWN_ASSERTION\", assertion_id, \"revision\")\n        replacement = dict(replacement)\n        replacement.setdefault(\"supersedes\", [assertion_id])\n        self.assertions = [replacement if x[\"id\"] == replacement[\"id\"] else x for x in self.assertions] + ([] if replacement[\"id\"] in rows else [replacement])\n        _validate_assertions(self.assertions)\n        self.current_results.clear()\n\n    def evaluate(self, request: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        evidence = select_evidence(self.assertions, request[\"cutoff\"], mode=request.get(\"evidence_view\", \"latest_available\"),\n                                   system_as_of=request.get(\"system_as_of\"), timezone_name=request.get(\"timezone\"),\n                                   date_only_policy=request.get(\"date_only_policy\"), harmonisations=request.get(\"harmonisations\", ()))\n        source_context = self.contexts[request[\"source_context\"]]\n        target_context = self.contexts[request[\"target_context\"]]\n        mapping = compatible_context(source_context, target_context, self.mappings, at=request.get(\"as_of\"))\n        admitted = []\n        for row in request.get(\"uncertainty\", ()):\n            admitted.append(admit_uncertainty(row, known_records=self.uncertainty))\n            self.uncertainty[row[\"id\"]] = admitted[-1]\n        resolution = resolve_bullet_debt(request[\"constituents\"], request[\"query\"], approximation=request.get(\"approximation\"))\n        result = {\"evidence\": evidence, \"mapping\": mapping, \"uncertainty\": admitted, \"resolution\": resolution,\n                  \"input_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, default=str).encode()).hexdigest()}\n        key = request.get(\"result_id\", \"current\")\n        self.current_results[key] = result\n        return result\n\n\n__all__ = [\"P06Error\", \"Context\", \"MappingRule\", \"compatible_context\", \"map_context\", \"check_partition\",\n           \"select_evidence\", \"subtract_cumulative\", \"admit_uncertainty\", \"guard_information_view\",\n           \"DebtConstituent\", \"interest_certificate\", \"resolve_bullet_debt\", \"P06Engine\"]\nPY\npython3 -m py_compile scripts/context_chronology_v1.py\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > scripts/context_chronology_v1.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Bounded P06 context, chronology, uncertainty and resolution runtime.\n\nThe profile is intentionally explicit: it uses exact \"'``Fraction`` arithmetic,\nGregorian half-open periods, finite populations, and a fixed-rate unhedged bullet\ndebt resolver.  Every rejection has a stable ``P06Error.code``.  This module\nchecks structural and computational contracts; it does not certify accounting\neligibility or the truth of retained source evidence.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import date, datetime, time, timedelta, timezone\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom types import MappingProxyType\nfrom typing import Any, Iterable, Mapping, Sequence\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo, ZoneInfoNotFoundError\n\n\nclass P06Error(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"A rejected P06 operation with a stable diagnostic code.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, code: str, message: str, *, location: str = \"\"):\n        self.code, self.location, self.message = code, location, message\n        suffix = f\" at {location}\" if location else \"\"\n        super().__init__(f\"{code}{suffix}: {message}\")\n\n\ndef fail(code: str, message: str, location: str = \"\") -> None:\n    raise P06Error(code, message, location=location)\n\n\ndef _fraction(value: Any, where: str = \"value\") -> Fraction:\n    if isinstance(value, Fraction):\n        return value\n    if isinstance(value, bool):\n        fail(\"INVALID_RATIONAL\", \"boolean is not a scalar\", where)\n    try:\n        if isinstance(value, int):\n            return Fraction(value)\n        if isinstance(value, str):\n            return Fraction(value)\n        if isinstance(value, float):\n            # Floats are rejected to keep exactness explicit.\n            fail(\"INEXACT_RATIONAL\", \"float input is not accepted\", where)\n        if isinstance(value, Mapping) and set(value) == {\"n\", \"d\"}:\n            q = Fraction(int(value[\"n\"]), int(value[\"d\"]))\n            if int(value[\"d\"]) <= 0:\n                fail(\"INVALID_RATIONAL\", \"denominator must be positive\", where)\n            if {\"n\": str(q.numerator), \"d\": str(q.denominator)} != {\n                \"n\": str(value[\"n\"]), \"d\": str(value[\"d\"])\n            }:\n                fail(\"NONCANONICAL_RATIONAL\", \"fraction must be reduced\", where)\n            return q\n    except (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError) as exc:\n        fail(\"INVALID_RATIONAL\", str(exc), where)\n    fail(\"INVALID_RATIONAL\", \"expected an integer or canonical rational\", where)\n\n\ndef _iso_date(value: Any, where: str) -> date:\n    if not isinstance(value, str):\n        fail(\"INVALID_DATE\", \"date must be YYYY-MM-DD\", where)\n    try:\n        parsed = date.fromisoformat(value)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        fail(\"INVALID_DATE\", str(exc), where)\n    if parsed.isoformat() != value:\n        fail(\"INVALID_DATE\", \"noncanonical ISO date\", where)\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _instant(value: Any, where: str) -> datetime:\n    if not isinstance(value, str):\n        fail(\"INVALID_TIMESTAMP\", \"timestamp must be an ISO string\", where)\n    try:\n        parsed = datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\"))\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        fail(\"INVALID_TIMESTAMP\", str(exc), where)\n    if parsed.tzinfo is None:\n        fail(\"MISSING_TIMEZONE\", \"timestamp requires an explicit timezone\", where)\n    return parsed\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Context:\n    concept: str\n    entity: str\n    perimeter: str\n    perimeter_version: str\n    basis: str\n    measurement: str\n    unit: str\n    currency: str\n    calendar: str\n    dimensions: tuple[tuple[str, str], ...] = ()\n    gross_net: str = \"gross\"\n    parent: str | None = None\n    group: str | None = None\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> \"Context\":\n        required = (\"concept\", \"entity\", \"perimeter\", \"perimeter_version\", \"basis\",\n                    \"measurement\", \"unit\", \"currency\", \"calendar\", \"dimensions\", \"gross_net\")\n        for key in required:\n            if key not in row:\n                fail(\"MISSING_CONTEXT_FIELD\", f\"missing {key}\", \"context\")\n        dims = row[\"dimensions\"]\n        if not isinstance(dims, Mapping):\n            fail(\"INVALID_DIMENSIONS\", \"dimensions must be an object\", \"context.dimensions\")\n        if any(not isinstance(k, str) or not isinstance(v, str) for k, v in dims.items()):\n            fail(\"INVALID_DIMENSIONS\", \"dimension keys and values must be strings\", \"context.dimensions\")\n        if row[\"gross_net\"] not in {\"gross\", \"net\"}:\n            fail(\"INVALID_GROSS_NET\", \"gross_net must be gross or net\", \"context.gross_net\")\n        return cls(*(str(row[k]) for k in required[:9]),\n                   tuple(sorted((str(k), str(v)) for k, v in dims.items())),\n                   str(row[\"gross_net\"]), row.get(\"parent\"), row.get(\"group\"))\n\n    def as_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        return {\n            \"concept\": self.concept, \"entity\": self.entity, \"perimeter\": self.perimeter,\n            \"perimeter_version\": self.perimeter_version, \"basis\": self.basis,\n            \"measurement\": self.measurement, \"unit\": self.unit, \"currency\": self.currency,\n            \"calendar\": self.calendar, \"dimensions\": dict(self.dimensions),\n            \"gross_net\": self.gross_net, \"parent\": self.parent, \"group\": self.group,\n        }\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass MappingRule:\n    source_concept: str\n    target_concept: str\n    kind: str = \"equivalent\"\n    source_context: str | None = None\n    target_context: str | None = None\n    effective_start: date | None = None\n    effective_end: date | None = None\n    conversion: str | None = None\n    provenance: tuple[str, ...] = ()\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> \"MappingRule\":\n        if not row.get(\"provenance\"):\n            fail(\"MAPPING_PROVENANCE_REQUIRED\", \"mapping provenance is required\", \"mapping\")\n        start = _iso_date(row[\"effective_start\"], \"mapping.effective_start\") if row.get(\"effective_start\") else None\n        end = _iso_date(row[\"effective_end\"], \"mapping.effective_end\") if row.get(\"effective_end\") else None\n        if start and end and end <= start:\n            fail(\"INVALID_MAPPING_WINDOW\", \"effective end must follow start\", \"mapping\")\n        kind = row.get(\"kind\", \"equivalent\")\n        if kind not in {\"equivalent\", \"component\", \"reclassification\"}:\n            fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_MAPPING\", f\"unsupported mapping kind {kind}\", \"mapping\")\n        return cls(str(row[\"source_concept\"]), str(row[\"target_concept\"]), kind,\n                   row.get(\"source_context\"), row.get(\"target_context\"), start, end,\n                   row.get(\"conversion\"), tuple(str(x) for x in row[\"provenance\"]))\n\n    def active(self, when: date | None) -> bool:\n        if when is None:\n            return self.effective_start is None and self.effective_end is None\n        return ((self.effective_start is None or when >= self.effective_start) and\n                (self.effective_end is None or when < self.effective_end))\n\n\ndef _context_mismatch(a: Context, b: Context) -> tuple[str, str] | None:\n    fields = (\"entity\", \"perimeter\", \"perimeter_version\", \"basis\", \"measurement\", \"unit\",\n              \"currency\", \"calendar\", \"dimensions\", \"gross_net\", \"parent\", \"group\")\n    for field_name in fields:\n        if getattr(a, field_name) != getattr(b, field_name):\n            return field_name, getattr(a, field_name).__repr__() + \" != \" + getattr(b, field_name).__repr__()\n    if a.concept != b.concept:\n        return \"concept\", repr(a.concept) + \" != \" + repr(b.concept)\n    return None\n\n\ndef _check_mapping_graph(rules: Sequence[MappingRule]) -> None:\n    graph: dict[str, set[str]] = {}\n    for rule in rules:\n        graph.setdefault(rule.source_concept, set()).add(rule.target_concept)\n    state: dict[str, int] = {}\n    def visit(node: str) -> None:\n        state[node] = 1\n        for nxt in graph.get(node, ()):\n            if state.get(nxt) == 1:\n                fail(\"MAPPING_CYCLE\", \"mapping graph contains a cycle\", node)\n            if state.get(nxt) != 2:\n                visit(nxt)\n        state[node] = 2\n    for node in graph:\n        if state.get(node, 0) == 0:\n            visit(node)\n\n\ndef compatible_context(source: Context | Mapping[str, Any], target: Context | Mapping[str, Any],\n                       rules: Sequence[MappingRule | Mapping[str, Any]] = (),\n                       *, at: str | date | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Return a mapping witness or reject a context mismatch.\"\"\"\n    a = source if isinstance(source, Context) else Context.from_dict(source)\n    b = target if isinstance(target, Context) else Context.from_dict(target)\n    when = _iso_date(at, \"mapping.at\") if isinstance(at, str) else at\n    parsed = [x if isinstance(x, MappingRule) else MappingRule.from_dict(x) for x in rules]\n    _check_mapping_graph(parsed)\n    mismatch = _context_mismatch(a, b)\n    if mismatch is None:\n        return {\"status\": \"compatible\", \"kind\": \"identity\", \"source\": a.as_dict(), \"target\": b.as_dict()}\n    field_name, detail = mismatch\n    if field_name == \"concept\":\n        eligible = [r for r in parsed if r.source_concept == a.concept and r.target_concept == b.concept and r.active(when)]\n        if not eligible:\n            fail(\"CONTEXT_MISMATCH\", f\"concept mismatch {detail} requires an explicit active mapping\", field_name)\n        rule = eligible[0]\n        if rule.kind == \"equivalent\" and (rule.conversion or \"\") not in {\"\", \"none\"}:\n            fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_MEASUREMENT_CONVERSION\", \"equivalent mapping cannot convert measurements\", field_name)\n        if rule.source_context and rule.source_context != a.entity:\n            fail(\"MAPPING_SOURCE_CONTEXT_MISMATCH\", \"mapping source context does not match\", field_name)\n        if rule.target_context and rule.target_context != b.entity:\n            fail(\"MAPPING_TARGET_CONTEXT_MISMATCH\", \"mapping target context does not match\", field_name)\n        return {\"status\": \"compatible\", \"kind\": rule.kind, \"source\": a.as_dict(), \"target\": b.as_dict(),\n                \"provenance\": list(rule.provenance)}\n    codes = {\"perimeter\": \"PARENT_GROUP_MISMATCH\", \"perimeter_version\": \"PERIMETER_VERSION_MISMATCH\",\n             \"basis\": \"BASIS_MISMATCH\", \"measurement\": \"MEASUREMENT_MISMATCH\", \"currency\": \"CURRENCY_MISMATCH\",\n             \"calendar\": \"CALENDAR_MISMATCH\", \"gross_net\": \"GROSS_NET_MISMATCH\", \"dimensions\": \"DIMENSION_MISMATCH\",\n             \"entity\": \"ENTITY_MISMATCH\", \"unit\": \"UNIT_MISMATCH\", \"parent\": \"PARENT_GROUP_MISMATCH\", \"group\": \"PARENT_GROUP_MISMATCH\"}\n    fail(codes.get(field_name, \"CONTEXT_MISMATCH\"), f\"context field mismatch: {detail}\", field_name)\n\n\ndef map_context(source: Context | Mapping[str, Any], target: Context | Mapping[str, Any],\n                rules: Sequence[MappingRule | Mapping[str, Any]] = (), *, at: str | date | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return compatible_context(source, target, rules, at=at)\n\n\ndef check_partition(population: Iterable[str], members: Mapping[str, Iterable[str]], *,\n                    residual: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None, axis: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n    pop = list(population)\n    if len(pop) != len(set(pop)):\n        fail(\"DUPLICATE_POPULATION\", \"population identifiers must be unique\", axis)\n    universe = set(pop)\n    seen: dict[str, str] = {}\n    normalized: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n    for label, values in members.items():\n        vals = list(values)\n        if len(vals) != len(set(vals)):\n            fail(\"DUPLICATE_MEMBER\", f\"member repeated in {label}\", axis)\n        unknown = set(vals) - universe\n        if unknown:\n            fail(\"UNKNOWN_MEMBER\", f\"members outside population: {sorted(unknown)}\", axis)\n        for value in vals:\n            if value in seen:\n                fail(\"OVERLAPPING_PARTITION\", f\"{value} occurs in {seen[value]} and {label}\", axis)\n            seen[value] = label\n        normalized[label] = vals\n    missing = universe - set(seen)\n    if missing:\n        if not residual:\n            fail(\"INCOMPLETE_PARTITION\", f\"uncovered members: {sorted(missing)}\", axis)\n        residual_values = set(residual.get(\"members\", ()))\n        if residual_values != missing:\n            fail(\"INVALID_RESIDUAL\", \"residual must identify exactly uncovered members\", axis)\n        if not residual.get(\"known\", False):\n            fail(\"UNKNOWN_RESIDUAL\", \"unknown residual cannot yield an exact total\", axis)\n    if residual and set(residual.get(\"members\", ())) & set(seen):\n        fail(\"OVERLAPPING_PARTITION\", \"residual overlaps a named member\", axis)\n    return {\"status\": \"partitioned\", \"axis\": axis, \"population\": pop, \"members\": normalized,\n            \"residual\": dict(residual) if residual else None, \"covered\": len(seen), \"complete\": not missing}\n\n\ndef _availability(value: Any, *, timezone_name: str | None, date_only_policy: str | None, where: str) -> datetime:\n    if isinstance(value, datetime):\n        if value.tzinfo is None:\n            fail(\"MISSING_TIMEZONE\", \"timestamp requires timezone\", where)\n        return value\n    if isinstance(value, date):\n        value = value.isoformat()\n    if not isinstance(value, str):\n        fail(\"INVALID_AVAILABILITY\", \"availability must be date or timestamp\", where)\n    if \"T\" in value or \" \" in value:\n        return _instant(value, where)\n    d = _iso_date(value, where)\n    if date_only_policy != \"next_local_midnight\":\n        fail(\"DATE_ONLY_POLICY_REQUIRED\", \"date-only availability requires next_local_midnight\", where)\n    if not timezone_name:\n        fail(\"TIMEZONE_REQUIRED\", \"named timezone required for date-only availability\", where)\n    try:\n        zone = ZoneInfo(timezone_name)\n    except ZoneInfoNotFoundError:\n        fail(\"UNKNOWN_TIMEZONE\", timezone_name, where)\n    return datetime.combine(d + timedelta(days=1), time.min, zone)\n\n\ndef _validate_assertions(assertions: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]]) -> dict[str, Mapping[str, Any]]:\n    rows = {str(a.get(\"id\")): a for a in assertions}\n    if len(rows) != len(assertions) or None in rows:\n        fail(\"DUPLICATE_ASSERTION\", \"assertion identifiers must be unique\", \"assertions\")\n    for row in assertions:\n        if not row.get(\"source\"):\n            fail(\"MISSING_SOURCE\", \"assertion source is required\", str(row.get(\"id\")))\n        for parent in row.get(\"supersedes\", []):\n            if parent not in rows:\n                fail(\"DANGLING_SUPERSESSION\", f\"unknown superseded assertion {parent}\", str(row.get(\"id\")))\n            if parent == row[\"id\"]:\n                fail(\"SUPERSESSION_CYCLE\", \"assertion cannot supersede itself\", str(row[\"id\"]))\n    state: dict[str, int] = {}\n    def visit(key: str) -> None:\n        state[key] = 1\n        for parent in rows[key].get(\"supersedes\", []):\n            if state.get(parent) == 1:\n                fail(\"SUPERSESSION_CYCLE\", \"supersession graph contains a cycle\", key)\n            if state.get(parent) != 2:\n                visit(parent)\n        state[key] = 2\n    for key in rows:\n        if state.get(key, 0) == 0:\n            visit(key)\n    return rows\n\n\ndef select_evidence(assertions: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]], cutoff: str | datetime | date, *,\n                    mode: str = \"latest_available\", system_as_of: str | datetime | date | None = None,\n                    timezone_name: str | None = None, date_only_policy: str | None = None,\n                    harmonisations: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]] = ()) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    rows = _validate_assertions(assertions)\n    if mode not in {\"original\", \"latest_available\", \"harmonised\"}:\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_EVIDENCE_VIEW\", mode, \"mode\")\n    if isinstance(cutoff, datetime):\n        cut = cutoff if cutoff.tzinfo else fail(\"MISSING_TIMEZONE\", \"cutoff requires timezone\", \"cutoff\")\n    else:\n        cut = _availability(cutoff, timezone_name=timezone_name, date_only_policy=date_only_policy, where=\"cutoff\")\n    asof = None\n    if system_as_of is not None:\n        asof = system_as_of if isinstance(system_as_of, datetime) else _availability(system_as_of, timezone_name=timezone_name, date_only_policy=date_only_policy, where=\"system_as_of\")\n    eligible = []\n    unresolved = []\n    for row in assertions:\n        try:\n            available = _availability(row[\"available\"], timezone_name=timezone_name, date_only_policy=date_only_policy, where=f\"{row['\"'id']}.available\\\")\n            ingested = _availability(row.get(\\\"ingested\\\", row[\\\"available\\\"]), timezone_name=timezone_name, date_only_policy=date_only_policy, where=f\\\"{row['id']}.ingested\\\")\n        except P06Error:\n            raise\n        if available <= cut and (asof is None or ingested <= asof):\n            eligible.append(row)\n        if row.get(\\\"historical_byte_vintage\\\") in {None, \\\"not_established_by_this_inventory\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"}:\n            unresolved.append({\\\"id\\\": row[\\\"id\\\"], \\\"reason\\\": \\\"historical_byte_vintage_unestablished\\\"})\n    eligible_ids = {x[\\\"id\\\"] for x in eligible}\n    if mode == \\\"original\\\":\n        selected = [x for x in eligible if not any(parent in eligible_ids for parent in x.get(\\\"supersedes\\\", []))]\n        # Roots are the first available assertions in a lineage: remove rows that supersede them.\n        selected = [x for x in selected if not x.get(\\\"supersedes\\\")]\n    else:\n        superseded = {parent for x in eligible for parent in x.get(\\\"supersedes\\\", [])}\n        selected = [x for x in eligible if x[\\\"id\\\"] not in superseded]\n    transformations = []\n    if mode == \\\"harmonised\\\":\n        for h in harmonisations:\n            source = h.get(\\\"source_id\\\")\n            if source not in {x[\\\"id\\\"] for x in selected}:\n                continue\n            if h.get(\\\"review_decision\\\") \"'!= \"Accept\" or not h.get(\"provenance\"):\n                fail(\"HARMONISATION_NOT_REVIEWED\", \"harmonisation requires accepted review and provenance\", str(source))\n            if h.get(\"changes_basis\") or h.get(\"changes_measurement\"):\n                fail(\"HARMONISATION_CONTEXT_CHANGE\", \"harmonisation cannot replace basis or measurement\", str(source))\n            transformations.append({\"source_id\": source, \"target_id\": h.get(\"target_id\", source), \"provenance\": list(h[\"provenance\"])})\n    return {\"mode\": mode, \"cutoff\": str(cutoff), \"selected\": [dict(x) for x in selected],\n            \"selected_ids\": [x[\"id\"] for x in selected], \"eligible_ids\": sorted(eligible_ids),\n            \"unresolved\": unresolved, \"transformations\": transformations}\n\n\ndef _row_context(row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return json.dumps(row.get(\"context\", {}), sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n\n\ndef subtract_cumulative(total: Mapping[str, Any], earlier: Mapping[str, Any], *,\n                        revision_compatibility: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    for label, row in ((\"total\", total), (\"earlier\", earlier)):\n        if row.get(\"kind\") != \"cumulative\":\n            fail(\"YTD_REQUIRES_CUMULATIVE\", f\"{label} must be cumulative\", label)\n        if row.get(\"period\", {}).get(\"end\") is None:\n            fail(\"INVALID_PERIOD\", \"cumulative period requires exclusive end\", label)\n    if total.get(\"concept\") != earlier.get(\"concept\"):\n        fail(\"CONCEPT_MISMATCH\", \"flow concepts differ\", \"ytd\")\n    if _row_context(total) != _row_context(earlier):\n        fail(\"CONTEXT_MISMATCH\", \"cumulative contexts differ\", \"ytd\")\n    if total.get(\"calendar\") != earlier.get(\"calendar\"):\n        fail(\"CALENDAR_MISMATCH\", \"calendars differ\", \"ytd\")\n    tp, ep = total[\"period\"], earlier[\"period\"]\n    if tp.get(\"start\") != ep.get(\"start\"):\n        fail(\"PERIOD_START_MISMATCH\", \"cumulative periods must share a start\", \"ytd\")\n    tend, eend = _iso_date(tp[\"end\"], \"total.period.end\"), _iso_date(ep[\"end\"], \"earlier.period.end\")\n    if eend >= tend:\n        fail(\"NONNESTED_PERIOD\", \"earlier period must end before total\", \"ytd\")\n    tstart = _iso_date(tp[\"start\"], \"total.period.start\")\n    if _iso_date(ep[\"start\"], \"earlier.period.start\") != tstart:\n        fail(\"PERIOD_START_MISMATCH\", \"period starts differ\", \"ytd\")\n    tr = total.get(\"revision_id\"); er = earlier.get(\"revision_id\")\n    if tr != er:\n        allowed = revision_compatibility and revision_compatibility.get(\"accepted\")\n        if not allowed or not revision_compatibility.get(\"scope\") or not revision_compatibility.get(\"evidence\"):\n            fail(\"REVISION_INCOMPATIBLE\", \"subtraction requires a common revision or reviewed scoped exception\", \"ytd\")\n    amount = _fraction(total[\"amount\"], \"total.amount\") - _fraction(earlier[\"amount\"], \"earlier.amount\")\n    return {\"kind\": \"flow\", \"amount\": amount, \"period\": {\"start\": ep[\"end\"], \"end\": tp[\"end\"]},\n            \"concept\": total[\"concept\"], \"context\": total.get(\"context\"), \"calendar\": total[\"calendar\"],\n            \"provenance\": {\"operation\": \"cumulative_subtraction\", \"total_id\": total.get(\"id\"), \"earlier_id\": earlier.get(\"id\"),\n                           \"revision_id\": tr or er}}\n\n\n_SUPPORTED_MEASUREMENT_METHODS = {\"direct\", \"discounted_cash_flow\", \"observable_input\"}\n_SUPPORTED_MEASURES = {\"real_world\", \"pricing\"}\n\n\ndef _validate_joint_law(law: Any, where: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    atoms = law.get(\"atoms\") if isinstance(law, Mapping) else law\n    if not isinstance(atoms, list) or not atoms:\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"finite joint law needs atoms\", where)\n    ids = [a.get(\"id\") for a in atoms]\n    if any(not isinstance(x, str) for x in ids) or len(ids) != len(set(ids)):\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"atom IDs must be distinct\", where)\n    hypotheses = [a.get(\"hypothesis\") for a in atoms]\n    if any(not isinstance(h, Mapping) or not h for h in hypotheses):\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"complete scalar hypotheses are required\", where)\n    if len({json.dumps(h, sort_keys=True) for h in hypotheses}) != len(hypotheses):\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"joint hypotheses overlap\", where)\n    weights = [_fraction(a.get(\"weight\"), where) for a in atoms]\n    if any(w < 0 for w in weights) or sum(weights, Fraction()) != 1:\n        fail(\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\", \"weights must be nonnegative and sum to one\", where)\n    return [dict(a) for a in atoms]\n\n\ndef admit_uncertainty(record: Mapping[str, Any], *, known_records: Mapping[str, Mapping[str, Any]] | None = None,\n                      available_information: Iterable[str] = ()) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    kind = record.get(\"kind\")\n    fields = {\n        \"ExtractionReading\": (\"source\", \"locator\", \"review_decision\"),\n        \"HistoricalFact\": (\"evidence\", \"reason\"),\n        \"AccountingElection\": (\"package\", \"permitted_treatments\", \"election\", \"effective_date\", \"eligibility_evidence\"),\n        \"MeasurementEstimate\": (\"method\", \"measurement_date\", \"inputs\"),\n        \"BehaviourPolicy\": (\"policy\", \"information_set\", \"decision_time\"),\n        \"FutureInnovation\": (\"driver\", \"future_period\", \"scenario\", \"joint_law\", \"measure\"),\n    }\n    if kind not in fields:\n        fail(\"UNKNOWN_UNCERTAINTY_CATEGORY\", f\"unsupported category {kind!r}\", \"kind\")\n    for key in (\"id\", \"scope\", \"provenance\", \"dependencies\") + fields[kind]:\n        if key not in record or (key != \"dependencies\" and not record[key]):\n            fail(\"MISSING_ADMISSION_FIELD\", f\"missing admission field {key}\", str(record.get(\"id\", \"\")))\n    if not isinstance(record[\"provenance\"], list) or not isinstance(record[\"dependencies\"], list):\n        fail(\"INVALID_ADMISSION_LIST\", \"provenance and dependencies must be lists\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    known_records = known_records or {}\n    for dep in record[\"dependencies\"]:\n        if dep not in known_records:\n            fail(\"DANGLING_DEPENDENCY\", f\"unknown dependency {dep}\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"ExtractionReading\" and record[\"review_decision\"] != \"Accept\":\n        fail(\"READING_NOT_ACCEPTED\", \"reading requires accepted review\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"AccountingElection\" and record[\"election\"] not in record[\"permitted_treatments\"]:\n        fail(\"TREATMENT_NOT_PERMITTED\", \"election is outside package permissions\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"MeasurementEstimate\":\n        if record[\"method\"] not in _SUPPORTED_MEASUREMENT_METHODS:\n            fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_ESTIMATION_METHOD\", record[\"method\"], str(record[\"id\"]))\n        if not isinstance(record[\"inputs\"], Mapping) or any(v is None for v in record[\"inputs\"].values()):\n            fail(\"MISSING_ESTIMATE_INPUT\", \"measurement inputs must be available\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"BehaviourPolicy\":\n        if not isinstance(record[\"information_set\"], list):\n            fail(\"INVALID_INFORMATION_SET\", \"information_set must be a list\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n        if any(str(x).startswith(\"future_realised:\") for x in record[\"information_set\"]):\n            fail(\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\", \"future realised outcome is unavailable at decision time\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n    if kind == \"FutureInnovation\":\n        if record[\"measure\"] not in _SUPPORTED_MEASURES:\n            fail(\"INCOMPATIBLE_PROBABILITY_MEASURE\", \"measure must be real_world or pricing\", str(record[\"id\"]))\n        _validate_joint_law(record[\"joint_law\"], str(record[\"id\"]))\n    return dict(record)\n\n\ndef guard_information_view(view: Mapping[str, Any], *, event_time: str | date, request: str = \"exogenous_stress\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n    if request in {\"observational_conditioning\", \"structural_intervention\"}:\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_INFORMATION_OPERATION\", request, \"information_view\")\n    visible = set(view.get(\"visible\", ()))\n    future_stress = set(view.get(\"future_announced\", ()))\n    hidden = set(view.get(\"future_realised\", ()))\n    if hidden & visible:\n        fail(\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\", \"future realised outcomes cannot be visible\", \"information_view\")\n    if not view.get(\"measure_id\"):\n        fail(\"MISSING_PROBABILITY_MEASURE\", \"information view needs an explicit measure\", \"information_view\")\n    if view.get(\"pricing_measure_id\") and view[\"pricing_measure_id\"] == view[\"measure_id\"]:\n        fail(\"INCOMPATIBLE_PROBABILITY_MEASURE\", \"real-world and pricing measures must be distinct\", \"information_view\")\n    return {\"status\": \"accepted\", \"event_time\": str(event_time), \"visible\": sorted(visible),\n            \"future_announced\": sorted(future_stress), \"future_realised_hidden\": sorted(hidden),\n            \"measure_id\": view[\"measure_id\"], \"selection_changes_history\": False}\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass DebtConstituent:\n    id: str\n    principal: Fraction\n    rate: Fraction\n    maturity: Fraction\n    reset: str = \"fixed\"\n    hedge: str = \"unhedged\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> \"DebtConstituent\":\n        principal = _fraction(row.get(\"principal\"), f\"{row.get('\"'id')}.principal\\\")\n        if principal < 0:\n            fail(\\\"NEGATIVE_PRINCIPAL\\\", \\\"principal must be nonnegative\\\", str(row.get(\\\"id\\\")))\n        return cls(str(row[\\\"id\\\"]), principal, _fraction(row.get(\\\"rate\\\"), f\\\"{row.get('id')}.rate\\\"),\n                   _fraction(row.get(\\\"maturity\\\"), f\\\"{row.get('id')}.maturity\\\"), str(row.get(\\\"reset\\\", \\\"fixed\\\")), str(row.get(\\\"hedge\\\", \\\"unhedged\\\")))\n\n\ndef _query_signature(query: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(query, sort_keys=True, default=str, separators=(\\\",\\\", \\\":\\\")).encode()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef interest_certificate(constituents: Sequence[DebtConstituent], target_rate: Fraction | str | int,\n                         horizon: Fraction | str | int) -> dict[str, Fraction]:\n    T = _fraction(horizon, \\\"horizon\\\")\n    if T < 0:\n        fail(\\\"INVALID_HORIZON\\\", \\\"horizon must be nonnegative\\\", \\\"horizon\\\")\n    rstar = _fraction(target_rate, \\\"target_rate\\\")\n    exact = sum((c.principal * c.rate * T for c in constituents), Fraction())\n    approx = sum((c.principal * rstar * T for c in constituents), Fraction())\n    bound = T * sum((c.principal * abs(c.rate - rstar) for c in constituents), Fraction())\n    difference = abs(exact - approx)\n    if difference > bound:\n        fail(\\\"INVALID_APPROXIMATION_CERTIFICATE\\\", \\\"triangle-inequality bound is violated\\\", \\\"approximation\\\")\n    return {\\\"exact\\\": exact, \\\"approximate\\\": approx, \\\"error\\\": difference, \\\"bound\\\": bound}\n\n\ndef resolve_bullet_debt(constituents: Sequence[DebtConstituent | Mapping[str, Any]], query: Mapping[str, Any], *,\n                       previous: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None,\n                       approximation: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    rows = [x if isinstance(x, DebtConstituent) else DebtConstituent.from_dict(x) for x in constituents]\n    if not rows:\n        fail(\\\"EMPTY_DEBT_SET\\\", \\\"at least one constituent is required\\\", \\\"debt\\\")\n    required = (\\\"contract\\\", \\\"context\\\", \\\"evidence_view\\\", \\\"horizon\\\", \\\"scenario\\\", \\\"requested_outputs\\\", \\\"accrual_convention\\\", \\\"group_by\\\")\n    for key in required:\n        if key not in query:\n            fail(\\\"MISSING_QUERY_FIELD\\\", f\\\"missing {key}\\\", \\\"query\\\")\n    signature = _query_signature(query)\n    if previous is not None and previous.get(\\\"query_signature\\\") \"'!= signature:\n        fail(\"STALE_RESULT\", \"query changed; grouping sufficiency must be revalidated\", \"query\")\n    horizon = _fraction(query[\"horizon\"], \"query.horizon\")\n    if horizon < 0:\n        fail(\"INVALID_HORIZON\", \"horizon must be nonnegative\", \"query.horizon\")\n    if query[\"scenario\"] not in {\"base\", \"announced_stress\"}:\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_SCENARIO\", str(query[\"scenario\"]), \"query.scenario\")\n    if query[\"accrual_convention\"] != \"simple_actual_fraction\":\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_ACCRUAL\", str(query[\"accrual_convention\"]), \"query.accrual_convention\")\n    if not isinstance(query[\"requested_outputs\"], list) or not query[\"requested_outputs\"]:\n        fail(\"MISSING_OUTPUT_REQUEST\", \"requested_outputs must be nonempty\", \"query\")\n    dimensions = (\"rate\", \"maturity\", \"reset\", \"hedge\")\n    group_by = set(query[\"group_by\"])\n    if not group_by <= set(dimensions):\n        fail(\"UNSUPPORTED_GROUP_DIMENSION\", \"group_by contains unsupported dimension\", \"query.group_by\")\n    for dim in dimensions:\n        values = {getattr(c, dim) for c in rows}\n        if len(values) > 1 and dim not in group_by:\n            fail(\"GROUPING_INSUFFICIENT\", f\"dimension {dim} varies but is not grouped\", \"query.group_by\")\n    for c in rows:\n        if c.hedge != \"unhedged\":\n            fail(\"HEDGED_DEBT_UNSUPPORTED\", \"only unhedged debt is supported\", c.id)\n        if c.reset != \"fixed\":\n            fail(\"RESET_UNSUPPORTED\", \"only fixed reset is supported\", c.id)\n        if c.maturity < horizon:\n            fail(\"MATURITY_CROSSING\", \"maturity crosses the requested horizon\", c.id)\n    groups: dict[tuple[Any, ...], list[DebtConstituent]] = {}\n    for c in rows:\n        key = tuple(getattr(c, dim) if dim in group_by else \"homogeneous\" for dim in dimensions)\n        groups.setdefault(key, []).append(c)\n    output: dict[str, Any] = {}\n    if \"interest\" in query[\"requested_outputs\"]:\n        output[\"interest\"] = sum((c.principal * c.rate * horizon for c in rows), Fraction())\n    if \"principal\" in query[\"requested_outputs\"]:\n        output[\"principal\"] = sum((c.principal for c in rows), Fraction())\n    result = {\"status\": \"resolved\", \"query_signature\": signature,\n              \"query\": json.loads(json.dumps(query, default=str)), \"groups\": [\n                  {\"key\": [str(x) for x in key], \"constituent_ids\": [c.id for c in members],\n                   \"principal\": sum((c.principal for c in members), Fraction()),\n                   \"interest\": sum((c.principal * c.rate * horizon for c in members), Fraction())}\n                  for key, members in groups.items()],\n              \"outputs\": output, \"constituent_ids\": [c.id for c in rows], \"fresh\": True}\n    if approximation is not None:\n        if not approximation.get(\"scope\") or approximation.get(\"scope\") != \"fixed_rate_interest\" or not approximation.get(\"evidence\"):\n            fail(\"APPROXIMATION_EVIDENCE_REQUIRED\", \"declared scope and evidence are required\", \"approximation\")\n        cert = interest_certificate(rows, approximation.get(\"target_rate\"), horizon)\n        tolerance = _fraction(approximation.get(\"tolerance\"), \"approximation.tolerance\")\n        declared = _fraction(approximation.get(\"error_bound\"), \"approximation.error_bound\")\n        if tolerance < 0 or declared < cert[\"error\"] or declared > tolerance or declared < cert[\"bound\"]:\n            fail(\"APPROXIMATION_BOUND_INVALID\", \"declared bound must cover exact error and certificate within tolerance\", \"approximation\")\n        result[\"approximation\"] = {k: str(v) for k, v in cert.items()} | {\"tolerance\": str(tolerance), \"declared_error_bound\": str(declared)}\n    return result\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass P06Engine:\n    contexts: dict[str, Context] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    mappings: list[MappingRule] = field(default_factory=list)\n    assertions: list[dict[str, Any]] = field(default_factory=list)\n    uncertainty: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    current_results: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    preserved_results: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = field(default_factory=dict)\n\n    def add_context(self, identifier: str, context: Context | Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n        if identifier in self.contexts:\n            fail(\"DUPLICATE_CONTEXT\", identifier, identifier)\n        self.contexts[identifier] = context if isinstance(context, Context) else Context.from_dict(context)\n\n    def add_mapping(self, rule: MappingRule | Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n        self.mappings.append(rule if isinstance(rule, MappingRule) else MappingRule.from_dict(rule))\n        _check_mapping_graph(self.mappings)\n\n    def add_assertion(self, row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n        self.assertions.append(dict(row))\n        _validate_assertions(self.assertions)\n\n    def revise(self, assertion_id: str, replacement: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n        rows = {x[\"id\"]: x for x in self.assertions}\n        if assertion_id not in rows:\n            fail(\"UNKNOWN_ASSERTION\", assertion_id, \"revision\")\n        replacement = dict(replacement)\n        replacement.setdefault(\"supersedes\", [assertion_id])\n        self.assertions = [replacement if x[\"id\"] == replacement[\"id\"] else x for x in self.assertions] + ([] if replacement[\"id\"] in rows else [replacement])\n        _validate_assertions(self.assertions)\n        self.current_results.clear()\n\n    def evaluate(self, request: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        evidence = select_evidence(self.assertions, request[\"cutoff\"], mode=request.get(\"evidence_view\", \"latest_available\"),\n                                   system_as_of=request.get(\"system_as_of\"), timezone_name=request.get(\"timezone\"),\n                                   date_only_policy=request.get(\"date_only_policy\"), harmonisations=request.get(\"harmonisations\", ()))\n        source_context = self.contexts[request[\"source_context\"]]\n        target_context = self.contexts[request[\"target_context\"]]\n        mapping = compatible_context(source_context, target_context, self.mappings, at=request.get(\"as_of\"))\n        admitted = []\n        for row in request.get(\"uncertainty\", ()):\n            admitted.append(admit_uncertainty(row, known_records=self.uncertainty))\n            self.uncertainty[row[\"id\"]] = admitted[-1]\n        resolution = resolve_bullet_debt(request[\"constituents\"], request[\"query\"], approximation=request.get(\"approximation\"))\n        result = {\"evidence\": evidence, \"mapping\": mapping, \"uncertainty\": admitted, \"resolution\": resolution,\n                  \"input_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, default=str).encode()).hexdigest()}\n        key = request.get(\"result_id\", \"current\")\n        self.current_results[key] = result\n        return result\n\n\n__all__ = [\"P06Error\", \"Context\", \"MappingRule\", \"compatible_context\", \"map_context\", \"check_partition\",\n           \"select_evidence\", \"subtract_cumulative\", \"admit_uncertainty\", \"guard_information_view\",\n           \"DebtConstituent\", \"interest_certificate\", \"resolve_bullet_debt\", \"P06Engine\"]\nPY\npython3 -m py_compile scripts/context_chronology_v1.py\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tests/test_accounting_p06.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Deterministic P06 conformance tests with independent arithmetic/set oracles.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport copy\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport unittest\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \\\"scripts\\\"))\nfrom context_chronology_v1 import (  # noqa: E402\n    Context, DebtConstituent, MappingRule, P06Engine, P06Error,\n    admit_uncertainty, check_partition, compatible_context, guard_information_view,\n    interest_certificate, resolve_bullet_debt, select_evidence, subtract_cumulative,\n)\n\n\ndef ctx(**overrides):\n    row = {\n        \\\"concept\\\": \\\"revenue\\\", \\\"entity\\\": \\\"Acme\\\", \\\"perimeter\\\": \\\"Acme\\\", \\\"perimeter_version\\\": \\\"2026\\\",\n        \\\"basis\\\": \\\"GAAP\\\", \\\"measurement\\\": \\\"historical_cost\\\", \\\"unit\\\": \\\"USD\\\", \\\"currency\\\": \\\"USD\\\",\n        \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"dimensions\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": \\\"retail\\\"}, \\\"gross_net\\\": \\\"gross\\\",\n    }\n    row.update(overrides)\n    return Context.from_dict(row)\n\n\ndef assertions():\n    return [\n        {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1-original\\\", \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"120\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}, \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-08-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2025-08-02\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [], \\\"source\\\": \\\"fixture:original\\\", \\\"historical_byte_vintage\\\": \\\"unknown\\\"},\n        {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1-revised\\\", \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"110\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}, \\\"available\\\": \\\"2026-02-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2026-02-02\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"h1-original\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"fixture:revision\\\", \\\"historical_byte_vintage\\\": \\\"unknown\\\"},\n        {\\\"id\\\": \\\"fy25\\\", \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"260\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"}, \\\"available\\\": \\\"2026-02-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2026-02-02\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [], \\\"source\\\": \\\"fixture:annual\\\", \\\"historical_byte_vintage\\\": \\\"unknown\\\"},\n    ]\n\n\nclass ContextPartitionTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_equivalent_context_mapping_and_spelling_preserved(self):\n        source, target = ctx(concept=\\\"sales\\\"), ctx(concept=\\\"revenue\\\")\n        rule = MappingRule(\\\"sales\\\", \\\"revenue\\\", provenance=(\\\"fixture:review\\\",))\n        witness = compatible_context(source, target, [rule], at=\\\"2026-01-01\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\\\"kind\\\"], \\\"equivalent\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\\\"source\\\"][\\\"concept\\\"], \\\"sales\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\\\"target\\\"][\\\"concept\\\"], \\\"revenue\\\")\n\n    def test_context_rejects_parent_basis_measurement_currency_calendar_gross_net(self):\n        for field, a, b, code in [\n            (\\\"perimeter\\\", \\\"Acme\\\", \\\"Group\\\", \\\"PARENT_GROUP_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"perimeter_version\\\", \\\"2026\\\", \\\"2025\\\", \\\"PERIMETER_VERSION_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"basis\\\", \\\"GAAP\\\", \\\"IFRS\\\", \\\"BASIS_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"measurement\\\", \\\"historical_cost\\\", \\\"fair_value\\\", \\\"MEASUREMENT_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"currency\\\", \\\"USD\\\", \\\"EUR\\\", \\\"CURRENCY_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"calendar\\\", \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"fiscal_445\\\", \\\"CALENDAR_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"gross_net\\\", \\\"gross\\\", \\\"net\\\", \\\"GROSS_NET_MISMATCH\\\"),\n        ]:\n            with self.subTest(field=field):\n                with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, code):\n                    compatible_context(ctx(**{field: a}), ctx(**{field: b}))\n\n    def test_expired_cycle_and_measurement_conversion_rejected(self):\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"CONTEXT_MISMATCH\\\"):\n            compatible_context(ctx(concept=\\\"a\\\"), ctx(concept=\\\"b\\\"), [MappingRule(\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\", effective_end=date(2025, 1, 1), provenance=(\\\"x\\\",))], at=\\\"2026-01-01\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"MAPPING_CYCLE\\\"):\n            compatible_context(ctx(concept=\\\"a\\\"), ctx(concept=\\\"b\\\"), [MappingRule(\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\", provenance=(\\\"x\\\",)), MappingRule(\\\"b\\\", \\\"a\\\", provenance=(\\\"y\\\",))])\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"UNSUPPORTED_MEASUREMENT_CONVERSION\\\"):\n            compatible_context(ctx(concept=\\\"a\\\"), ctx(concept=\\\"b\\\", measurement=\\\"fair_value\\\"), [MappingRule(\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\", conversion=\\\"USD_to_EUR\\\", provenance=(\\\"x\\\",))])\n\n    def test_partition_independent_enumeration_and_unknown_residual(self):\n        ok = check_partition([\\\"e1\\\", \\\"e2\\\", \\\"e3\\\"], {\\\"north\\\": [\\\"e1\\\"], \\\"south\\\": [\\\"e2\\\", \\\"e3\\\"]}, axis=\\\"geo\\\")\n        self.assertTrue(ok[\\\"complete\\\"])\n        for members in ({\\\"north\\\": [\\\"e1\\\", \\\"e2\\\"], \\\"south\\\": [\\\"e2\\\", \\\"e3\\\"]}, {\\\"north\\\": [\\\"e1\\\"]}):\n            with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"OVERLAPPING_PARTITION|INCOMPLETE_PARTITION\\\"):\n                check_partition([\\\"e1\\\", \\\"e2\\\", \\\"e3\\\"], members, axis=\\\"geo\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"UNKNOWN_RESIDUAL\\\"):\n            check_partition([\\\"e1\\\", \\\"e2\\\"], {\\\"north\\\": [\\\"e1\\\"]}, residual={\\\"members\\\": [\\\"e2\\\"], \\\"known\\\": False}, axis=\\\"geo\\\")\n\n    def test_partition_population_and_axis_prevent_double_counting(self):\n        self.assertEqual(check_partition([\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\"], {\\\"x\\\": [\\\"a\\\"], \\\"y\\\": [\\\"b\\\"]}, axis=\\\"product\\\")[\\\"axis\\\"], \\\"product\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"OVERLAPPING_PARTITION\\\"):\n            check_partition([\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\"], {\\\"x\\\": [\\\"a\\\"], \\\"all\\\": [\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\"]}, axis=\\\"product\\\")\n\n\nclass ChronologyYTDTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_original_latest_and_harmonised_selection(self):\n        rows = assertions()\n        original = select_evidence(rows, \\\"2025-12-31\\\", mode=\\\"original\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(original[\\\"selected_ids\\\"], [\\\"h1-original\\\"])\n        latest = select_evidence(rows, \\\"2026-12-31\\\", mode=\\\"latest_available\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(set(latest[\\\"selected_ids\\\"]), {\\\"h1-revised\\\", \\\"fy25\\\"})\n        harm = select_evidence(rows, \\\"2026-12-31\\\", mode=\\\"harmonised\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\", harmonisations=[{\\\"source_id\\\": \\\"h1-revised\\\", \\\"target_id\\\": \\\"sales-harmonised\\\", \\\"review_decision\\\": \\\"Accept\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": [\\\"review:1\\\"]}])\n        self.assertEqual(harm[\\\"transformations\\\"][0][\\\"target_id\\\"], \\\"sales-harmonised\\\")\n        self.assertTrue(harm[\\\"unresolved\\\"])\n\n    def test_cutoff_ingestion_and_date_only_boundary(self):\n        row = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"d\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [], \\\"source\\\": \\\"x\\\"}\n        before = select_evidence([row], \\\"2025-01-01T23:59:59+00:00\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n        equal = select_evidence([row], \\\"2025-01-02T00:00:00+00:00\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(before[\\\"selected_ids\\\"], [])\n        self.assertEqual(equal[\\\"selected_ids\\\"], [\\\"d\\\"])\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"DATE_ONLY_POLICY_REQUIRED\\\"):\n            select_evidence([row], \\\"2025-01-02\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"TIMEZONE_REQUIRED\\\"):\n            select_evidence([row], \\\"2025-01-02\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n\n    def test_dangling_and_cyclic_supersession_rejected(self):\n        bad = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"z\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"x\\\"}\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"DANGLING_SUPERSESSION\\\"):\n            select_evidence([bad], \\\"2026-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\")\n        a = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"b\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"x\\\"}\n        b = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"b\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"a\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"x\\\"}\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"SUPERSESSION_CYCLE\\\"):\n            select_evidence([a, b], \\\"2026-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\")\n\n    def test_ytd_valid_subtraction_uses_revised_h1(self):\n        result = subtract_cumulative(\n            {\\\"id\\\": \\\"fy\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 260, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"context\\\": {\\\"entity\\\": \\\"A\\\"}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r2\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"}},\n            {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 110, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"context\\\": {\\\"entity\\\": \\\"A\\\"}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r2\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}},\n        )\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"amount\\\"], F(150))\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"period\\\"], {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"})\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"REVISION_INCOMPATIBLE\\\"):\n            subtract_cumulative({\\\"id\\\": \\\"fy\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 260, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"context\\\": {\\\"entity\\\": \\\"A\\\"}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r2\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"}}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 120, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"context\\\": {\\\"entity\\\": \\\"A\\\"}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r1\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}})\n\n    def test_ytd_rejects_instant_start_and_nonnested(self):\n        base = {\\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 1, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"x\\\", \\\"context\\\": {}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"g\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}}\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"YTD_REQUIRES_CUMULATIVE\\\"):\n            subtract_cumulative({**base, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"instant\\\"}, base)\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"PERIOD_START_MISMATCH\\\"):\n            subtract_cumulative({**base, \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-02-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"}}, base)\n\n\nclass UncertaintyTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def _base(self, kind, **extra):\n        row = {\\\"id\\\": kind.lower(), \\\"kind\\\": kind, \\\"scope\\\": \\\"demo\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": [\\\"fixture\\\"], \\\"dependencies\\\": []}\n        row.update(extra)\n        return row\n\n    def test_all_six_categories_and_dependencies(self):\n        records = {}\n        cases = [\n            self._base(\\\"ExtractionReading\\\", source=\\\"doc\\\", locator=\\\"p1\\\", review_decision=\\\"Accept\\\"),\n            self._base(\\\"HistoricalFact\\\", evidence=\\\"doc\\\", reason=\\\"dated\\\"),\n            self._base(\\\"AccountingElection\\\", package=\\\"pkg\\\", permitted_treatments=[\\\"A\\\"], election=\\\"A\\\", effective_date=\\\"2025-01-01\\\", eligibility_evidence=\\\"memo\\\"),\n            self._base(\\\"MeasurementEstimate\\\", method=\\\"direct\\\", measurement_date=\\\"2025-01-01\\\", inputs={\\\"x\\\": 1}),\n            self._base(\\\"BehaviourPolicy\\\", policy=\\\"hold\\\", information_set=[\\\"past:price\\\"], decision_time=\\\"2025-01-01\\\"),\n            self._base(\\\"FutureInnovation\\\", driver=\\\"shock\\\", future_period=\\\"2026\\\", scenario=\\\"base\\\", joint_law={\\\"atoms\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"a\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\":{\\\"x\\\":0},\\\"weight\\\":\\\"1\\\"}]}, measure=\\\"real_world\\\"),\n        ]\n        for row in cases:\n            records[row[\\\"id\\\"]] = admit_uncertainty(row, known_records=records)\n        self.assertEqual(set(records), {x[\\\"id\\\"] for x in cases})\n\n    def test_uncertainty_negative_semantics(self):\n        b = self._base\n        for row, code in [\n            (b(\\\"ExtractionReading\\\", source=\\\"d\\\", locator=\\\"p\\\", review_decision=\\\"Reject\\\"), \\\"READING_NOT_ACCEPTED\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"AccountingElection\\\", package=\\\"p\\\", permitted_treatments=[\\\"A\\\"], election=\\\"B\\\", effective_date=\\\"x\\\", eligibility_evidence=\\\"e\\\"), \\\"TREATMENT_NOT_PERMITTED\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"MeasurementEstimate\\\", method=\\\"unknown\\\", measurement_date=\\\"x\\\", inputs={\\\"x\\\": 1}), \\\"UNSUPPORTED_ESTIMATION_METHOD\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"MeasurementEstimate\\\", method=\\\"direct\\\", measurement_date=\\\"x\\\", inputs={\\\"x\\\": None}), \\\"MISSING_ESTIMATE_INPUT\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"BehaviourPolicy\\\", policy=\\\"x\\\", information_set=[\\\"future_realised:y\\\"], decision_time=\\\"x\\\"), \\\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"FutureInnovation\\\", driver=\\\"x\\\", future_period=\\\"x\\\", scenario=\\\"x\\\", joint_law={\\\"atoms\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"a\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\":{\\\"x\\\":0},\\\"weight\\\":\\\"1/2\\\"}]}, measure=\\\"pricing\\\"), \\\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"Mystery\\\", x=\\\"x\\\"), \\\"UNKNOWN_UNCERTAINTY_CATEGORY\\\"),\n        ]:\n            with self.subTest(code=code), self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, code):\n                admit_uncertainty(row)\n\n    def test_information_view_blocks_leakage_and_unimplemented_modes(self):\n        accepted = guard_information_view({\\\"visible\\\": [\\\"past:x\\\"], \\\"future_announced\\\": [\\\"stress:y\\\"], \\\"future_realised\\\": [\\\"outcome:z\\\"], \\\"measure_id\\\": \\\"P\\\", \\\"pricing_measure_id\\\": \\\"Q\\\"}, event_time=\\\"2025-01-01\\\")\n        self.assertFalse(accepted[\\\"selection_changes_history\\\"])\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\\\"):\n            guard_information_view({\\\"visible\\\": [\\\"future_realised:z\\\"], \\\"measure_id\\\": \\\"P\\\"}, event_time=\\\"x\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"UNSUPPORTED_INFORMATION_OPERATION\\\"):\n            guard_information_view({\\\"visible\\\": [], \\\"measure_id\\\": \\\"P\\\"}, event_time=\\\"x\\\", request=\\\"structural_intervention\\\")\n\n\nclass ResolutionTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def rows(self):\n        return [DebtConstituent(\\\"a\\\", F(100), F(5, 100), F(2)), DebtConstituent(\\\"b\\\", F(50), F(7, 100), F(2))]\n\n    def query(self, **extra):\n        q = {\\\"contract\\\": \\\"bullet-v1\\\", \\\"context\\\": \\\"usd\\\", \\\"evidence_view\\\": \\\"latest_available\\\", \\\"horizon\\\": \\\"1\\\", \\\"scenario\\\": \\\"base\\\", \\\"requested_outputs\\\": [\\\"interest\\\", \\\"principal\\\"], \\\"accrual_convention\\\": \\\"simple_actual_fraction\\\", \\\"group_by\\\": [\\\"rate\\\", \\\"maturity\\\", \\\"reset\\\", \\\"hedge\\\"]}\n        q.update(extra)\n        return q\n\n    def test_exact_grouped_resolution_and_independent_oracle(self):\n        result = resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query())\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"outputs\\\"][\\\"interest\\\"], F(17, 2))\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"outputs\\\"][\\\"principal\\\"], F(150))\n        self.assertEqual(sum(g[\\\"interest\\\"] for g in result[\\\"groups\\\"]), F(17, 2))\n\n    def test_query_horizon_scenario_and_grouping_sufficiency(self):\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"GROUPING_INSUFFICIENT\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(group_by=[\\\"rate\\\", \\\"reset\\\", \\\"hedge\\\"]))\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"UNSUPPORTED_SCENARIO\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(scenario=\\\"future_realised\\\"))\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"MATURITY_CROSSING\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(horizon=\\\"3\\\"))\n\n    def test_approximation_requires_declared_error_evidence(self):\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"APPROXIMATION_EVIDENCE_REQUIRED\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(), approximation={\\\"target_rate\\\": \\\"0.06\\\", \\\"tolerance\\\": \\\"1\\\", \\\"error_bound\\\": \\\"1\\\"})\n        result = resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(), approximation={\\\"target_rate\\\": \\\"0.06\\\", \\\"tolerance\\\": \\\"1\\\", \\\"error_bound\\\": \\\"1/2\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"fixed_rate_interest\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"certificate:triangle\\\"]})\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"approximation\\\"][\\\"error\\\"], \\\"1/2\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"approximation\\\"][\\\"bound\\\"], \\\"1/2\\\")\n\n    def test_stale_result_and_unsupported_dynamics(self):\n        previous = resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query())\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"STALE_RESULT\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(horizon=\\\"2\\\"), previous=previous)\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"RESET_UNSUPPORTED\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt([DebtConstituent(\\\"a\\\", F(1), F(1, 10), F(2), reset=\\\"floating\\\")], self.query(group_by=[\\\"rate\\\", \\\"maturity\\\", \\\"reset\\\", \\\"hedge\\\"]))\n\n\nclass IntegrationTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_public_entrypoint_selects_maps_admits_and_resolves(self):\n        engine = P06Engine()\n        engine.add_context(\\\"source\\\", ctx(concept=\\\"sales\\\"))\n        engine.add_context(\\\"target\\\", ctx(concept=\\\"revenue\\\"))\n        engine.add_mapping({\\\"source_concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"target_concept\\\": \\\"revenue\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": [\\\"fixture:mapping\\\"]})\n        for row in assertions():\n            engine.add_assertion(row)\n        reading = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"read\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"ExtractionReading\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"demo\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": [\\\"fixture\\\"], \\\"dependencies\\\": [], \\\"source\\\": \\\"doc\\\", \\\"locator\\\": \\\"p1\\\", \\\"review_decision\\\": \\\"Accept\\\"}\n        request = {\\\"cutoff\\\": \\\"2026-12-31\\\", \\\"timezone\\\": \\\"UTC\\\", \\\"date_only_policy\\\": \\\"next_local_midnight\\\", \\\"evidence_view\\\": \\\"latest_available\\\", \\\"source_context\\\": \\\"source\\\", \\\"target_context\\\": \\\"target\\\", \\\"uncertainty\\\": [reading], \\\"constituents\\\": [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"principal\\\": \\\"100\\\", \\\"rate\\\": \\\"1/20\\\", \\\"maturity\\\": \\\"2\\\"}], \\\"query\\\": {\\\"contract\\\": \\\"bullet-v1\\\", \\\"context\\\": \\\"usd\\\", \\\"evidence_view\\\": \\\"latest_available\\\", \\\"horizon\\\": \\\"1\\\", \\\"scenario\\\": \\\"base\\\", \\\"requested_outputs\\\": [\\\"interest\\\"], \\\"accrual_convention\\\": \\\"simple_actual_fraction\\\", \\\"group_by\\\": [\\\"rate\\\", \\\"maturity\\\", \\\"reset\\\", \\\"hedge\\\"]}}\n        result = engine.evaluate(request)\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"resolution\\\"][\\\"outputs\\\"][\\\"interest\\\"], F(5))\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"mapping\\\"][\\\"kind\\\"], \\\"equivalent\\\")\n        engine.revise(\\\"h1-original\\\", {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1-new\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2026-03-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2026-03-02\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"h1-original\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"fixture:new\\\"})\n        self.assertFalse(engine.current_results)\n\n\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\n    unittest.main()\nPY\npython3 -m py_compile tests/test_accounting_p06.py\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python3 -B -m unittest tests/test_accounting_p06.py -v\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tests/test_accounting_p06.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Deterministic P06 conformance tests with independent arithmetic/set oracles.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport copy\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport unittest\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \\\"scripts\\\"))\nfrom context_chronology_v1 import (  # noqa: E402\n    Context, DebtConstituent, MappingRule, P06Engine, P06Error,\n    admit_uncertainty, check_partition, compatible_context, guard_information_view,\n    interest_certificate, resolve_bullet_debt, select_evidence, subtract_cumulative,\n)\n\n\ndef ctx(**overrides):\n    row = {\n        \\\"concept\\\": \\\"revenue\\\", \\\"entity\\\": \\\"Acme\\\", \\\"perimeter\\\": \\\"Acme\\\", \\\"perimeter_version\\\": \\\"2026\\\",\n        \\\"basis\\\": \\\"GAAP\\\", \\\"measurement\\\": \\\"historical_cost\\\", \\\"unit\\\": \\\"USD\\\", \\\"currency\\\": \\\"USD\\\",\n        \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"dimensions\\\": {\\\"segment\\\": \\\"retail\\\"}, \\\"gross_net\\\": \\\"gross\\\",\n    }\n    row.update(overrides)\n    return Context.from_dict(row)\n\n\ndef assertions():\n    return [\n        {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1-original\\\", \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"120\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}, \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-08-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2025-08-02\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [], \\\"source\\\": \\\"fixture:original\\\", \\\"historical_byte_vintage\\\": \\\"unknown\\\"},\n        {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1-revised\\\", \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"110\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}, \\\"available\\\": \\\"2026-02-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2026-02-02\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"h1-original\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"fixture:revision\\\", \\\"historical_byte_vintage\\\": \\\"unknown\\\"},\n        {\\\"id\\\": \\\"fy25\\\", \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"260\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"}, \\\"available\\\": \\\"2026-02-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2026-02-02\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [], \\\"source\\\": \\\"fixture:annual\\\", \\\"historical_byte_vintage\\\": \\\"unknown\\\"},\n    ]\n\n\nclass ContextPartitionTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_equivalent_context_mapping_and_spelling_preserved(self):\n        source, target = ctx(concept=\\\"sales\\\"), ctx(concept=\\\"revenue\\\")\n        rule = MappingRule(\\\"sales\\\", \\\"revenue\\\", provenance=(\\\"fixture:review\\\",))\n        witness = compatible_context(source, target, [rule], at=\\\"2026-01-01\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\\\"kind\\\"], \\\"equivalent\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\\\"source\\\"][\\\"concept\\\"], \\\"sales\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\\\"target\\\"][\\\"concept\\\"], \\\"revenue\\\")\n\n    def test_context_rejects_parent_basis_measurement_currency_calendar_gross_net(self):\n        for field, a, b, code in [\n            (\\\"perimeter\\\", \\\"Acme\\\", \\\"Group\\\", \\\"PARENT_GROUP_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"perimeter_version\\\", \\\"2026\\\", \\\"2025\\\", \\\"PERIMETER_VERSION_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"basis\\\", \\\"GAAP\\\", \\\"IFRS\\\", \\\"BASIS_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"measurement\\\", \\\"historical_cost\\\", \\\"fair_value\\\", \\\"MEASUREMENT_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"currency\\\", \\\"USD\\\", \\\"EUR\\\", \\\"CURRENCY_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"calendar\\\", \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"fiscal_445\\\", \\\"CALENDAR_MISMATCH\\\"),\n            (\\\"gross_net\\\", \\\"gross\\\", \\\"net\\\", \\\"GROSS_NET_MISMATCH\\\"),\n        ]:\n            with self.subTest(field=field):\n                with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, code):\n                    compatible_context(ctx(**{field: a}), ctx(**{field: b}))\n\n    def test_expired_cycle_and_measurement_conversion_rejected(self):\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"CONTEXT_MISMATCH\\\"):\n            compatible_context(ctx(concept=\\\"a\\\"), ctx(concept=\\\"b\\\"), [MappingRule(\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\", effective_end=date(2025, 1, 1), provenance=(\\\"x\\\",))], at=\\\"2026-01-01\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"MAPPING_CYCLE\\\"):\n            compatible_context(ctx(concept=\\\"a\\\"), ctx(concept=\\\"b\\\"), [MappingRule(\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\", provenance=(\\\"x\\\",)), MappingRule(\\\"b\\\", \\\"a\\\", provenance=(\\\"y\\\",))])\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"UNSUPPORTED_MEASUREMENT_CONVERSION\\\"):\n            compatible_context(ctx(concept=\\\"a\\\"), ctx(concept=\\\"b\\\", measurement=\\\"fair_value\\\"), [MappingRule(\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\", conversion=\\\"USD_to_EUR\\\", provenance=(\\\"x\\\",))])\n\n    def test_partition_independent_enumeration_and_unknown_residual(self):\n        ok = check_partition([\\\"e1\\\", \\\"e2\\\", \\\"e3\\\"], {\\\"north\\\": [\\\"e1\\\"], \\\"south\\\": [\\\"e2\\\", \\\"e3\\\"]}, axis=\\\"geo\\\")\n        self.assertTrue(ok[\\\"complete\\\"])\n        for members in ({\\\"north\\\": [\\\"e1\\\", \\\"e2\\\"], \\\"south\\\": [\\\"e2\\\", \\\"e3\\\"]}, {\\\"north\\\": [\\\"e1\\\"]}):\n            with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"OVERLAPPING_PARTITION|INCOMPLETE_PARTITION\\\"):\n                check_partition([\\\"e1\\\", \\\"e2\\\", \\\"e3\\\"], members, axis=\\\"geo\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"UNKNOWN_RESIDUAL\\\"):\n            check_partition([\\\"e1\\\", \\\"e2\\\"], {\\\"north\\\": [\\\"e1\\\"]}, residual={\\\"members\\\": [\\\"e2\\\"], \\\"known\\\": False}, axis=\\\"geo\\\")\n\n    def test_partition_population_and_axis_prevent_double_counting(self):\n        self.assertEqual(check_partition([\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\"], {\\\"x\\\": [\\\"a\\\"], \\\"y\\\": [\\\"b\\\"]}, axis=\\\"product\\\")[\\\"axis\\\"], \\\"product\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"OVERLAPPING_PARTITION\\\"):\n            check_partition([\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\"], {\\\"x\\\": [\\\"a\\\"], \\\"all\\\": [\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\"]}, axis=\\\"product\\\")\n\n\nclass ChronologyYTDTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_original_latest_and_harmonised_selection(self):\n        rows = assertions()\n        original = select_evidence(rows, \\\"2025-12-31\\\", mode=\\\"original\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(original[\\\"selected_ids\\\"], [\\\"h1-original\\\"])\n        latest = select_evidence(rows, \\\"2026-12-31\\\", mode=\\\"latest_available\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(set(latest[\\\"selected_ids\\\"]), {\\\"h1-revised\\\", \\\"fy25\\\"})\n        harm = select_evidence(rows, \\\"2026-12-31\\\", mode=\\\"harmonised\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\", harmonisations=[{\\\"source_id\\\": \\\"h1-revised\\\", \\\"target_id\\\": \\\"sales-harmonised\\\", \\\"review_decision\\\": \\\"Accept\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": [\\\"review:1\\\"]}])\n        self.assertEqual(harm[\\\"transformations\\\"][0][\\\"target_id\\\"], \\\"sales-harmonised\\\")\n        self.assertTrue(harm[\\\"unresolved\\\"])\n\n    def test_cutoff_ingestion_and_date_only_boundary(self):\n        row = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"d\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [], \\\"source\\\": \\\"x\\\"}\n        before = select_evidence([row], \\\"2025-01-01T23:59:59+00:00\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n        equal = select_evidence([row], \\\"2025-01-02T00:00:00+00:00\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(before[\\\"selected_ids\\\"], [])\n        self.assertEqual(equal[\\\"selected_ids\\\"], [\\\"d\\\"])\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"DATE_ONLY_POLICY_REQUIRED\\\"):\n            select_evidence([row], \\\"2025-01-02\\\", timezone_name=\\\"UTC\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"TIMEZONE_REQUIRED\\\"):\n            select_evidence([row], \\\"2025-01-02\\\", date_only_policy=\\\"next_local_midnight\\\")\n\n    def test_dangling_and_cyclic_supersession_rejected(self):\n        bad = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"z\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"x\\\"}\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"DANGLING_SUPERSESSION\\\"):\n            select_evidence([bad], \\\"2026-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\")\n        a = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"b\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"x\\\"}\n        b = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"b\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2025-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"a\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"x\\\"}\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"SUPERSESSION_CYCLE\\\"):\n            select_evidence([a, b], \\\"2026-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\\\")\n\n    def test_ytd_valid_subtraction_uses_revised_h1(self):\n        result = subtract_cumulative(\n            {\\\"id\\\": \\\"fy\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 260, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"context\\\": {\\\"entity\\\": \\\"A\\\"}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r2\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"}},\n            {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 110, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"context\\\": {\\\"entity\\\": \\\"A\\\"}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r2\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}},\n        )\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"amount\\\"], F(150))\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"period\\\"], {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"})\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"REVISION_INCOMPATIBLE\\\"):\n            subtract_cumulative({\\\"id\\\": \\\"fy\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 260, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"context\\\": {\\\"entity\\\": \\\"A\\\"}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r2\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"}}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 120, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"context\\\": {\\\"entity\\\": \\\"A\\\"}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"gregorian\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r1\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}})\n\n    def test_ytd_rejects_instant_start_and_nonnested(self):\n        base = {\\\"kind\\\": \\\"cumulative\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 1, \\\"concept\\\": \\\"x\\\", \\\"context\\\": {}, \\\"calendar\\\": \\\"g\\\", \\\"revision_id\\\": \\\"r\\\", \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-01-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-06-30\\\"}}\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"YTD_REQUIRES_CUMULATIVE\\\"):\n            subtract_cumulative({**base, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"instant\\\"}, base)\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"PERIOD_START_MISMATCH\\\"):\n            subtract_cumulative({**base, \\\"period\\\": {\\\"start\\\": \\\"2025-02-01\\\", \\\"end\\\": \\\"2025-12-31\\\"}}, base)\n\n\nclass UncertaintyTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def _base(self, kind, **extra):\n        row = {\\\"id\\\": kind.lower(), \\\"kind\\\": kind, \\\"scope\\\": \\\"demo\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": [\\\"fixture\\\"], \\\"dependencies\\\": []}\n        row.update(extra)\n        return row\n\n    def test_all_six_categories_and_dependencies(self):\n        records = {}\n        cases = [\n            self._base(\\\"ExtractionReading\\\", source=\\\"doc\\\", locator=\\\"p1\\\", review_decision=\\\"Accept\\\"),\n            self._base(\\\"HistoricalFact\\\", evidence=\\\"doc\\\", reason=\\\"dated\\\"),\n            self._base(\\\"AccountingElection\\\", package=\\\"pkg\\\", permitted_treatments=[\\\"A\\\"], election=\\\"A\\\", effective_date=\\\"2025-01-01\\\", eligibility_evidence=\\\"memo\\\"),\n            self._base(\\\"MeasurementEstimate\\\", method=\\\"direct\\\", measurement_date=\\\"2025-01-01\\\", inputs={\\\"x\\\": 1}),\n            self._base(\\\"BehaviourPolicy\\\", policy=\\\"hold\\\", information_set=[\\\"past:price\\\"], decision_time=\\\"2025-01-01\\\"),\n            self._base(\\\"FutureInnovation\\\", driver=\\\"shock\\\", future_period=\\\"2026\\\", scenario=\\\"base\\\", joint_law={\\\"atoms\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"a\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\":{\\\"x\\\":0},\\\"weight\\\":\\\"1\\\"}]}, measure=\\\"real_world\\\"),\n        ]\n        for row in cases:\n            records[row[\\\"id\\\"]] = admit_uncertainty(row, known_records=records)\n        self.assertEqual(set(records), {x[\\\"id\\\"] for x in cases})\n\n    def test_uncertainty_negative_semantics(self):\n        b = self._base\n        for row, code in [\n            (b(\\\"ExtractionReading\\\", source=\\\"d\\\", locator=\\\"p\\\", review_decision=\\\"Reject\\\"), \\\"READING_NOT_ACCEPTED\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"AccountingElection\\\", package=\\\"p\\\", permitted_treatments=[\\\"A\\\"], election=\\\"B\\\", effective_date=\\\"x\\\", eligibility_evidence=\\\"e\\\"), \\\"TREATMENT_NOT_PERMITTED\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"MeasurementEstimate\\\", method=\\\"unknown\\\", measurement_date=\\\"x\\\", inputs={\\\"x\\\": 1}), \\\"UNSUPPORTED_ESTIMATION_METHOD\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"MeasurementEstimate\\\", method=\\\"direct\\\", measurement_date=\\\"x\\\", inputs={\\\"x\\\": None}), \\\"MISSING_ESTIMATE_INPUT\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"BehaviourPolicy\\\", policy=\\\"x\\\", information_set=[\\\"future_realised:y\\\"], decision_time=\\\"x\\\"), \\\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"FutureInnovation\\\", driver=\\\"x\\\", future_period=\\\"x\\\", scenario=\\\"x\\\", joint_law={\\\"atoms\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"a\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\":{\\\"x\\\":0},\\\"weight\\\":\\\"1/2\\\"}]}, measure=\\\"pricing\\\"), \\\"INVALID_JOINT_LAW\\\"),\n            (b(\\\"Mystery\\\", x=\\\"x\\\"), \\\"UNKNOWN_UNCERTAINTY_CATEGORY\\\"),\n        ]:\n            with self.subTest(code=code), self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, code):\n                admit_uncertainty(row)\n\n    def test_information_view_blocks_leakage_and_unimplemented_modes(self):\n        accepted = guard_information_view({\\\"visible\\\": [\\\"past:x\\\"], \\\"future_announced\\\": [\\\"stress:y\\\"], \\\"future_realised\\\": [\\\"outcome:z\\\"], \\\"measure_id\\\": \\\"P\\\", \\\"pricing_measure_id\\\": \\\"Q\\\"}, event_time=\\\"2025-01-01\\\")\n        self.assertFalse(accepted[\\\"selection_changes_history\\\"])\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"FUTURE_INFORMATION_LEAKAGE\\\"):\n            guard_information_view({\\\"visible\\\": [\\\"future_realised:z\\\"], \\\"measure_id\\\": \\\"P\\\"}, event_time=\\\"x\\\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"UNSUPPORTED_INFORMATION_OPERATION\\\"):\n            guard_information_view({\\\"visible\\\": [], \\\"measure_id\\\": \\\"P\\\"}, event_time=\\\"x\\\", request=\\\"structural_intervention\\\")\n\n\nclass ResolutionTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def rows(self):\n        return [DebtConstituent(\\\"a\\\", F(100), F(5, 100), F(2)), DebtConstituent(\\\"b\\\", F(50), F(7, 100), F(2))]\n\n    def query(self, **extra):\n        q = {\\\"contract\\\": \\\"bullet-v1\\\", \\\"context\\\": \\\"usd\\\", \\\"evidence_view\\\": \\\"latest_available\\\", \\\"horizon\\\": \\\"1\\\", \\\"scenario\\\": \\\"base\\\", \\\"requested_outputs\\\": [\\\"interest\\\", \\\"principal\\\"], \\\"accrual_convention\\\": \\\"simple_actual_fraction\\\", \\\"group_by\\\": [\\\"rate\\\", \\\"maturity\\\", \\\"reset\\\", \\\"hedge\\\"]}\n        q.update(extra)\n        return q\n\n    def test_exact_grouped_resolution_and_independent_oracle(self):\n        result = resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query())\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"outputs\\\"][\\\"interest\\\"], F(17, 2))\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"outputs\\\"][\\\"principal\\\"], F(150))\n        self.assertEqual(sum(g[\\\"interest\\\"] for g in result[\\\"groups\\\"]), F(17, 2))\n\n    def test_query_horizon_scenario_and_grouping_sufficiency(self):\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"GROUPING_INSUFFICIENT\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(group_by=[\\\"rate\\\", \\\"reset\\\", \\\"hedge\\\"]))\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"UNSUPPORTED_SCENARIO\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(scenario=\\\"future_realised\\\"))\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"MATURITY_CROSSING\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(horizon=\\\"3\\\"))\n\n    def test_approximation_requires_declared_error_evidence(self):\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"APPROXIMATION_EVIDENCE_REQUIRED\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(), approximation={\\\"target_rate\\\": \\\"0.06\\\", \\\"tolerance\\\": \\\"1\\\", \\\"error_bound\\\": \\\"1\\\"})\n        result = resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(), approximation={\\\"target_rate\\\": \\\"0.06\\\", \\\"tolerance\\\": \\\"1\\\", \\\"error_bound\\\": \\\"1/2\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"fixed_rate_interest\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"certificate:triangle\\\"]})\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"approximation\\\"][\\\"error\\\"], \\\"1/2\\\")\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"approximation\\\"][\\\"bound\\\"], \\\"1/2\\\")\n\n    def test_stale_result_and_unsupported_dynamics(self):\n        previous = resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query())\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"STALE_RESULT\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt(self.rows(), self.query(horizon=\\\"2\\\"), previous=previous)\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(P06Error, \\\"RESET_UNSUPPORTED\\\"):\n            resolve_bullet_debt([DebtConstituent(\\\"a\\\", F(1), F(1, 10), F(2), reset=\\\"floating\\\")], self.query(group_by=[\\\"rate\\\", \\\"maturity\\\", \\\"reset\\\", \\\"hedge\\\"]))\n\n\nclass IntegrationTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_public_entrypoint_selects_maps_admits_and_resolves(self):\n        engine = P06Engine()\n        engine.add_context(\\\"source\\\", ctx(concept=\\\"sales\\\"))\n        engine.add_context(\\\"target\\\", ctx(concept=\\\"revenue\\\"))\n        engine.add_mapping({\\\"source_concept\\\": \\\"sales\\\", \\\"target_concept\\\": \\\"revenue\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": [\\\"fixture:mapping\\\"]})\n        for row in assertions():\n            engine.add_assertion(row)\n        reading = {\\\"id\\\": \\\"read\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"ExtractionReading\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"demo\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": [\\\"fixture\\\"], \\\"dependencies\\\": [], \\\"source\\\": \\\"doc\\\", \\\"locator\\\": \\\"p1\\\", \\\"review_decision\\\": \\\"Accept\\\"}\n        request = {\\\"cutoff\\\": \\\"2026-12-31\\\", \\\"timezone\\\": \\\"UTC\\\", \\\"date_only_policy\\\": \\\"next_local_midnight\\\", \\\"evidence_view\\\": \\\"latest_available\\\", \\\"source_context\\\": \\\"source\\\", \\\"target_context\\\": \\\"target\\\", \\\"uncertainty\\\": [reading], \\\"constituents\\\": [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"principal\\\": \\\"100\\\", \\\"rate\\\": \\\"1/20\\\", \\\"maturity\\\": \\\"2\\\"}], \\\"query\\\": {\\\"contract\\\": \\\"bullet-v1\\\", \\\"context\\\": \\\"usd\\\", \\\"evidence_view\\\": \\\"latest_available\\\", \\\"horizon\\\": \\\"1\\\", \\\"scenario\\\": \\\"base\\\", \\\"requested_outputs\\\": [\\\"interest\\\"], \\\"accrual_convention\\\": \\\"simple_actual_fraction\\\", \\\"group_by\\\": [\\\"rate\\\", \\\"maturity\\\", \\\"reset\\\", \\\"hedge\\\"]}}\n        result = engine.evaluate(request)\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"resolution\\\"][\\\"outputs\\\"][\\\"interest\\\"], F(5))\n        self.assertEqual(result[\\\"mapping\\\"][\\\"kind\\\"], \\\"equivalent\\\")\n        engine.revise(\\\"h1-original\\\", {\\\"id\\\": \\\"h1-new\\\", \\\"available\\\": \\\"2026-03-01\\\", \\\"ingested\\\": \\\"2026-03-02\\\", \\\"supersedes\\\": [\\\"h1-original\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"fixture:new\\\"})\n        self.assertFalse(engine.current_results)\n\n\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\n    unittest.main()\nPY\npython3 -m py_compile tests/test_accounting_p06.py\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python3 -B -m unittest tests/test_accounting_p06.py -v\n\"","aggregated_output":"test_cutoff_ingestion_and_date_only_boundary (tests.test_accounting_p06.ChronologyYTDTests.test_cutoff_ingestion_and_date_only_boundary) ... ok\ntest_dangling_and_cyclic_supersession_rejected (tests.test_accounting_p06.ChronologyYTDTests.test_dangling_and_cyclic_supersession_rejected) ... ok\ntest_original_latest_and_harmonised_selection (tests.test_accounting_p06.ChronologyYTDTests.test_original_latest_and_harmonised_selection) ... ok\ntest_ytd_rejects_instant_start_and_nonnested (tests.test_accounting_p06.ChronologyYTDTests.test_ytd_rejects_instant_start_and_nonnested) ... ok\ntest_ytd_valid_subtraction_uses_revised_h1 (tests.test_accounting_p06.ChronologyYTDTests.test_ytd_valid_subtraction_uses_revised_h1) ... ok\ntest_context_rejects_parent_basis_measurement_currency_calendar_gross_net (tests.test_accounting_p06.ContextPartitionTests.test_context_rejects_parent_basis_measurement_currency_calendar_gross_net) ... ok\ntest_equivalent_context_mapping_and_spelling_preserved (tests.test_accounting_p06.ContextPartitionTests.test_equivalent_context_mapping_and_spelling_pre